window.FWN_SHADOW_SLAVE_CHAPTERS=(window.FWN_SHADOW_SLAVE_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":3201,"title":"Chapter 3201 A Land Without Monsters","paragraphs":["The city was vast and prosperous, built with not only utility in mind, but beauty as well. That was why the city lord's stronghold resembled a temple more than a fortress, with marble pillars supporting carved pediments and exquisite statues watching over the verdant gardens. That was not to say that it wasn't a fortress, though — just from one glance, Shadow could see how easy it was to defend.","The soldiers escorted him and Noctis to the heart of the stronghold, where a great reception hall rested in the shadows, radiant beams of sunlight spilling through high windows.","There, they met a placid man who looked to be in his thirties, wearing a simple white tunic and an azure toga. His auburn hair spilled to his shoulders, supported by a golden band, and his eyes were both enlightened and clear.","Despite how young the man looked, Shadow could feel the weight of wisdom in his gaze — a wisdom that could only be earned by living a long life and experiencing many things. Even without peering into the man's soul, he knew that the lord of the city was a Transcendent who had weathered hundreds of years.","Noctis had called him an old man, after all... granted, all men seemed old to that inexperienced youth.","Speaking of Noctis, the closer they came to the city lord's stronghold, the more nervous he looked. Now that they stood directly in front of the lord, there were beads of sweat rolling down his face.","Despite that, the lord himself seemed calm enough. If anything, his faint smile looked friendly.","“Welcome, Beast of Twilight... and his friend.\"","The lord's gaze lingered on Shadow for a few moments, then moved on. He probably guessed that the young man accompanying Noctis was not a mundane person, but chose not to question his identity just yet. Noctis remained silent for a few moments, then gave the lord an awkward bow.","\"Beast of Twilight greets Arelen, the Altar Sage.\"","Then, he cleared his throat and forced out a few more words.","\"Listen, Lord Arelen... about the last time... it was all a misunderstanding! Let me explain myself?\"","Shadow spared him a brief glance, amused by the spirited youth's sudden docility. It seemed he still knew how to respect his elders, at least.","The city lord — Transcendent Arelen, seemingly known as the Altar Sage — just chuckled and waved a hand dismissively.","“No need to explain. It's all in the past... a small matter.\"","He clasped his hands behind his back and walked toward Noctis and Shadow, giving the soldiers a nod to leave.","“Rather, I simply invited you here to have a welcoming feast and perhaps discuss a few matters. I couldn't let an honored guest stay at an inn, could I? So, please, follow me.\"","Noctis seemed quite surprised by Arelen's amicable attitude. He glanced at Shadow nervously, and once the ruler of the city walked past them, leaned closer to whisper:","\"I don't like this, Shadow! If something happens, let's bolt!\"","Shadow simply shrugged, turning to follow their host.","Despite the worries of the young Transcendent, Lord Arelen was true to his word. Soon enough, they arrived at a hall where a lavish feast had already been prepared. As they enjoyed the food, musicians played soft melodies, and nimble dancers performed a beautiful dance in front of them.","The atmosphere was harmonious, as if there was no bad blood between Arelen and Noctis, and as if the city outside was not drowning in a strange tension.","The Altar Sage inquired about the journey Noctis had undertaken, showing a hint of curiosity.","\"So, Noctis, how have you fared in your recent travels? I heard that you ventured to discover the source of the dreadful darkness that had devoured the Shadow people. Were you successful in eliminating that ancient curse?\"","Noctis let out a nervous laugh.","He glanced briefly at Shadow, then said:","\"Well... the darkness is gone now, and sunlight washes over the bones of those poor folks once again. So, one could say that this humble hero was a little bit successful. However, only ruins and desolation remain in that land, while beyond the ruins, the forests are teeming with terrifying horrors. The curse is gone, but... uh... I wouldn't say that I vanquished it. I just happened to be lucky.\"","The Altar Sage seemed a little surprised.","\"The darkness is gone? What a great achievement! For generations, many outstanding heroes had attempted to liberate that distant realm from its clutches. None had succeeded, yet you managed to destroy it alone. Truly a feat worthy of Noctis, the Beast of Twilight!\"","Noctis smiled weakly.","\"Y—yes... truly a feat worthy of me! Let's not talk about it anymore, though. You're making me feel shy.\"","Shadow was pretty sure that there wasn't a shy bone in the young wastrel's body, but he chose to stay silent.","Not long after that, though, he finally spoke for the first time. Turning to the ruler of this land, he asked:","\"On the way here, we noticed that the streets of your city are unusually crowded, Lord Arelen. People huddle in makeshift tents and wear anxious expressions. If I may ask, has something unfortunate transpired?\"","He had a feeling that the tense atmosphere of the city was the real reason why the Altar Sage had invited Noctis to come, and even seemed to forgive his past transgressions. If anything, it looked like Arelen wanted to placate Noctis, for whatever reason.","So, everything they had talked about until now was merely a preamble to the real conversation.","The Altar Sage remained silent for a few moments, looking at Noctis and Shadow with a faint smile, then sighed.","His smile slowly drained away.","\"Indeed, something unfortunate has happened. I am afraid that my lands will be attacked quite soon, so the people of the surrounding towns and villages were forced to seek shelter behind its walls.\"","Noctis almost spat his wine and stared at the older Transcendent, surprised.","“Attacked? What kind of abomination has crawled out of its den, and how powerful must it be for all the people of your land to flee?\"","The Creature of Corruption had to be extremely fearsome, considering that a powerful and experienced Transcendent like the Altar Sage had not gone out to battle it. If it was too strong for a single Transcendent to defeat... that could explain why Arelen was being so friendly to Noctis, who was a fierce warrior despite his young age.","Shadow took a sip of his wine, savoring its flavor. He had never tasted wine before — not in this lifetime, at least — and was finding its rich bitterness, brightened by a hint of sweetness, quite refreshing.","‘If it's just a Creature of Corruption, there is no need for concern.'","However, the long silence of the Altar Sage made him frown slightly.","He had a feeling that matters were not that simple, after all.","Eventually, Arelen slowly shook his head.","\"There is no abomination, young Noctis. Instead, it is Lady Irian, the Blade of Dawn, who has assembled an army to besiege my city and lay claim to my lands.\"","Noctis looked stunned.","He remained silent for a long while, as if struggling to understand what the Altar Sage had said. Finally, he let out a bewildered laugh.","“You must be joking, Lord Arelen. Isn't Lady Irian known for her valor, wisdom, and virtue? And aren't the two of you old comrades who have battled countless Creatures of Corruption side by side? Everyone knows that with the Altar Sage defending this side of the river and the Blade of Dawn defending the other, no Nightmare Creature can threaten the livelihoods of humans in this realm. The two of you have lived in peace for centuries, so why would she suddenly attack?\"","Slowly, his expression was twisted with anger.","Putting his cup down, Noctis shook his head.","\"Before that, since when do Transcendent heroes wage war against each other? In this world, we humans are barely holding our own against the Creatures of Corruption! Countless people still suffer from the tyranny of abominable monsters, and our lands are not enough to sustain our numbers! If we want to live, if we want to prosper, we need to push the forces of Corruption back and conquer land. We must fight together, not against each other! So why...\"","His voice gradually grew quiet, and Noctis huffed in dismay.","\"Why are the two of you at each other's throats?\"","The Altar Sage studied Noctis for a few moments, then glanced away and sighed with a wistful smile.","\"You are young, Beast of Twilight. The world you described... it truly did exist, once, when I was young. But everything changes.\"","He glanced at Noctis and smiled.","\"Let me ask you this, Noctis. Do our actions as slayers of monsters have no consequence?\"","As Noctis frowned in confusion, Arelen chuckled and shook his head.","\"It is true that we humans are entangled in a war with the Creatures of Corruption, struggling for dominance over the world. However... after all these centuries, after all these victories, after hundreds of years of the glorious Age of Heroes, how could everything remain the same?\"","He gestured to the musicians playing their instruments and the maidens dancing in front of them.","“When I was young, my city was besieged by terrifying horrors on all sides. Our fields were burned and poisoned every year, and countless men died protecting the walls. I was one of the men defending the walls, as well. Then, I grew more powerful. I grew wiser. I faced those horrors, slaying them one after another — until there was no one left to threaten my city, and its fields sprawled across a vast and prosperous land. The same is true for Irian.\"","Arelen sighed.","“But, Noctis, what do you think happens when we humans have no enemy left to fight? Do we settle down to enjoy peace, forgetting the meaning of violence? Or do we start to look around, noticing what other humans possess, and wishing to own it instead? To be the strongest, the greatest... the most glorious.\"","Shadow tilted his head, listening to the seasoned Transcendent with interest. Human nature was indeed restless, and it was of some interest to the Shadow, so he enjoyed this unexpected insight.","Noctis, however, was not having a good time at all. Instead, the more Arelen spoke, the angrier the young man seemed.","“What are you trying to say, Altar Sage? That the more we heroes slay monsters, the more human blood will be spilled? That once there are no monsters to kill, humans will simply start killing each other? So... the more successful we heroes are, the more horrible human lives will become? And there will never be peace?\"","He scoffed.","“Ha! You are being ridiculous. Preposterous! You have lost sight of what it means to be Transcendent, old man.\"","Arelen studied him for a long while. Eventually, he smiled faintly.","“Of course, there will be peace. In this realm, there will be peace when only one Transcendent rules it. When there is no one left to challenge the ruler’s will, then there'll be peace.\"","He glanced away and added, his voice distant:","“That was how it has been since the dawn of time. Even the mythical First Kingdom only existed for as long as White Abyss ruled over it like a mortal goddess, unreachable and insurmountable, impossible to challenge or depose. Once their sovereign abandoned the people of the First Kingdom, it was quickly torn apart by the ambitions of powerful men.\"","Arelen's expression turned solemn.","\"The world is changing, young Noctis. Slowly but inevitably, it transforms. Humans were weak and few in number before. We struggled to survive in a world full of Corruption — Awakened warriors were rare, and Ascended champions were like a precious treasure. Each Transcendent was like a living legend. But now... how many of us Transcendent heroes are there? How many powerful abominations remain, and how vast a land do they still control?\"","He shook his head.","“Much more than that, now that humanity has accumulated knowledge and gained some strength, Transcendence is not the pinnacle of power anymore. There are already those who defy the heavens to become Supreme... to become sovereigns like those ancient demigods, Kanakht and White Abyss. And hearing of their deeds, which Transcendent doesn't want to attain Supremacy?\"","Noctis glared at him with a dark expression. Eventually, he uttered through gritted teeth:","\"Is Supremacy so important? So desirable? So alluring that those who are meant to protect humans will gather armies and spill human blood instead?\"","The Altar Sage glanced at him with a hint of amusement.","Eventually, he said:","\"Of course, it is.\"","His noble face suddenly seemed older than it was.","\"After all, how can we not desire Supremacy? You are kin to Beast God, Noctis, and even if I am merely a distant descendant, there is a drop of divine blood in my veins as well. We live in a world where gods walk the earth. When looking at the gods, how can we not desire to become gods ourselves?\"","Arelen glanced away with a wistful expression.","“To live for thousands of years instead of hundreds, or even for eternity. To see our people prosper endlessly. To reach for the heavens and bask in their radiance... to conquer them and sit upon a celestial throne. With no common enemy to stand in our way, with no Creatures of Corruption to threaten our lands, who can resist the call of the heavens, the desire to become immortal?\"","Noctis scoffed.","\"Immortality does sound like a lot of fun, but not if it's achieved through despicable means. Surely, Lady Irian is not leading her army to your city because she wishes to live forever.\"","The Altar Sage glanced down.","After a while, he said quietly:","\"True. Supremacy, immortality — those are not insignificant, but they are too distant to be the real cause of this calamity. The real reason for this war, young Noctis... is you.\"","Noctis froze, then raised his eyebrows in disbelief.","\"Me? What are you talking about, old man?! How could I have caused a war between you two?\"","The Altar Sage smiled sadly.","“Did you not slay the Horror of the Viridian Marsh, that Corrupted Tyrant who had haunted the borders of my and Irian's lands for generations? For centuries, both of us tried and failed to kill it. And yet, all those months ago when you visited my city, young hero, you ventured into the marsh and fought a great battle, ending that abomination's profane existence and slaughtering its brood.\"","Noctis frowned.","\"I did, yes! And let me tell you, it was quite a ghastly experience! But so what?\"","Arelen glanced away.","“With the Tyrant gone and its minions either slain or scattered, the miraculously fertile lands near the estuary of the river, as well as precious minerals hidden in the depths of the marsh, were left without a master. Naturally, both Irian and I wanted to lay claim to that land.”","Noctis continued to frown, his expression stormy.","“Couldn't you have split it fairly?\"","The Altar Sage smiled.","“I thought we could. But then, before consulting with me and coming to an agreement, Irian sent settlers to establish a settlement in those newly liberated lands. Because her people needed food.\"","His smile widened a little, becoming somewhat fierce.","“But don't my people need food as well, Beast of Twilight? And those precious minerals, don't my warriors need stronger blades and armor so that they could protect my people, too?\"","His smile dimmed.","Arelen remained silent for a long while, then sighed.","\"So, I ordered my warriors to raze the settlement and slaughter Irian's people. And now, she's coming to exact her vengeance.”","He pursed his lips, a hint of bitterness finding its way into his placid eyes.","“It seems that without the Creatures of Corruption pressing down on us, this vast realm is too small for both Irian and me. One of us must fall.\"","Looking at Noctis, he lingered for a moment. As the music grew quiet and the dancers retreated, the Altar Sage said:","\"Beast of Twilight. Even if it wasn't your intention, the war between Arelen the Altar Sage and Irian, the Blade of Dawn, is happening in part because of what you've done. So, when she arrives... I want you to help me end the war.\"","His words were solemn.","“I want you to help me kill Irian, sunder her army, and bring this land to peace.\""]},{"number":3202,"title":"Chapter 3202 Conflict of Interests","paragraphs":["“That old fool has lost his mind!\"","Having parted with Arelen, Noctis and Shadow had returned to the inn. Noctis had not given the Altar Sage an answer, and the older Transcendent had not insisted on receiving one either — he simply implored the two of them to consider his request. Judging by how angry Noctis was, though, it did not seem like he was inclined to see Arelen's offer in good light.","“Fighting over land? With Lady Irian, of all people?! What was he thinking, ordering his warriors to slaughter her people?!\"","Noctis looked at Shadow, his eyes glinting fiercely.","“And what, the bastard has the gall to blame me for his misdeeds? Asking me to help him kill the Blade of Dawn? Bah! The Altar Sage was supposed to be an icon of wisdom and temperance. Where the hell were his wisdom and temperance when he provoked this war?!\"","The young man cursed quietly, then uttered with a dark expression:","\"If someone has to be killed for this war to stop, shouldn't it be him instead of Lady Irian? He's at fault, so if I were to kill someone, it'd be him!\"","Snuggle, who had climbed out of Shadow's pocket, jumped down to the table and sat down, using an overturned teacup as a chair.","Looking up at the rattled youth, she waved a hand.","\"Calm down.\"","Noctis threw a glare in her direction and scoffed.","\"Whatever do you mean? I'm calm! So calm! I am the calmest person in this realm, no less!\"","Shadow shook his head with a sigh and sat as well.","\"Snuggle is right. You should calm down and think about things clearly. They might not be what they seem to be.\"","Noctis remained silent for a few moments, breathing heavily, then cursed again and pulled back a chair. Crashing down on it, he pierced Shadow with a burning look and asked:","\"How so?\"","Shadow lingered for a bit, then shrugged.","\"The Altar Sage, the Blade of Dawn... you know them better, but neither of them is simple. They are Transcendent rulers with centuries of experience, so do you really think that either one would have acted rashly and recklessly? Would Lady Irian have failed to account for the possibility of Lord Arelen's violent response? Would Arelen have failed to foresee what his actions were certain to cause?\"","Noctis stared at him silently, a hint of confusion finding its way into his gaze. Finally, he grimaced.","“What do you mean?\"","Shadow shook his head.","\"These two are shrewd and seasoned. One doesn't survive long in your line of work without those qualities, definitely not for centuries. So, why do you think Irian claimed the land without even trying to negotiate with Arelen, and why did Arelen — who is supposed to be wise and patient — throw a bloody tantrum and ruthlessly wipe out her settlers?\"","Noctis lingered for a moment or two, then scoffed.","\"How should I know? Greed, ambition? Arelen certainly had a lot to say about his reasons, but I don't buy any of it for a second. He seems to have gone mad!\"","Shadow sighed and shook his head again, then looked at Snuggle.","\"What do you think?\"","Snuggle scratched her head, her small onyx eyes glinting darkly.","Eventually, she said:","“I guess what Arelen said was mostly true. But also a complete lie. It's true that once these lands weren't under threat anymore, with most powerful abominations gone, a conflict between two bordering kingdoms became all but inevitable. But it's a lie that Noctis is the cause — he might have contributed a little, but both Arelen and Irian had to have been contemplating moving against each other for a long time.\"","The little doll lowered her head and added dejectedly:","“All people want to live, after all. And once their lives are not in danger anymore, they always want to live well. But there's never enough nice things for everyone, so someone ends up living better, while others end up looking up at them with envy.\"","Shadow nodded.","“It seems like this war is the result of several unfortunate decisions and miscalculations, Arelen's rash order to slaughter the settlers most of all. But in truth, both he and Irian knew what they were doing. Irian knew that claiming that land without even trying to negotiate would provoke Arelen — she was testing his patience. And Arelen showed her that he had no patience at all, knowing all too well what kind of response that would provoke.\"","He smiled darkly.","“They both got what they wanted. Irian got a true justification to attack and conquer Arelen's city...\"","Noctis frowned.","“Wait, what do you mean the old fool knew what would happen? Even if you are right and the Blade of Dawn was hoping he would give her a reason to invade, what does Arelen get from having her attack his lands?\"","Shadow shrugged.","\"What does he get? Quite a valuable thing, actually. He gets the right to choose the battlefield. After all, Noctis, if you knew that a clash with a powerful adversary was inevitable, would you want to meet them in an open field, or under the walls of your city, which you have been fortifying for centuries?\"","Noctis leaned back, a stunned expression on his face.","He remained silent for a long while, then glanced at Shadow and Snuggle somberly.","\"I guess he is wise, after all. Just... deplorable.\"","A bitter scoff escaped from his lips.","“No wonder that old fool believed he could rope me into his conflict with Lady Irian. He probably thought that a young fool like me would be easy to wrap around his finger... and the worst thing is, he wasn't that wrong.\"","Snuggle giggled.","\"Actually, he probably never hoped to convince you to side with him.\"","Noctis blinked a couple of times.","“What? Then why did he spend so much time trying to convince me?\"","She shook her head and pointed at him with her chubby hand.","\"Think about it, fool! A battle with another Transcendent is only a few days away, and suddenly, another Transcendent arrives in your city — purely by coincidence, he claims. Obviously, Arelen wanted to see if that Irian lady had already recruited you into helping her get rid of him. If you weren't so easy to read and he was left with the smallest hint of doubt back there, he'd probably killed you already — well, perhaps not. Maybe he'd just give you a good beating and lock you up somewhere until this whole war was over. He does seem kind of nice, after all.”","Noctis scoffed.","\"Nice... yes, sure.”","He fell silent, a dark expression on his face. After some time, Noctis laughed and shook his head in dismay.","“I just don't get it! Why? Why do they have to do this? Alright, let's say that there's fertile land and marsh treasures to be had. Do they have to go to war for that? Why can't they just... I don't know... marry and solve their problems in the bedroom! Then, their child would inherit both kingdoms, and everyone can live in peace. The process would be much more enjoyable for all involved parties, needless to say!\"","Hearing that, Snuggle couldn't help but laugh.","Shadow smiled faintly, as well.","He did not say anything immediately, but then shrugged.","\"I think killing each other is both simpler and more straightforward.\"","Noctis gave him a dismayed look.","“Gods, who am I asking? You're a Creature of Shadow! All you shadows ever think about is death.”","Shadow studied him for a moment, then sighed.","“Are you that different?\"","Leaning forward, he picked up the kettle and poured himself some tea.","\"Sure, we shadows are born from death. But don't you heroes spend your entire lives slaughtering Creatures of Corruption? It doesn't matter whether your cause is noble or not. After a lifetime of battles and bloodshed, it's not that surprising that Arelen and Irian grew accustomed to seeing the world through the prism of violence. That is what they know best, after all.\"","He lingered for a moment, then added:","\"I have to give them some credit, though. They could have started a slow, exhausting conflict — one side biting a piece out of the other, the other responding in kind. There would have been endless skirmishes, slow escalation, more and more corpses on both sides. Until, one day, generations later, either Arelen or Irian finally won a significant advantage to wipe the other out.\"","Shadow shook his head.","\"But Arelen didn't want that, so he went for the swiftest solution and ordered Irian's settlement to be entirely destroyed — he wanted this war of theirs to start and end in the span of a single battle. That is something, at least.”","Noctis looked at him darkly.","\"Oh, wow. How noble of him.\"","Finally, he sighed and stood up, walking to the window to take in the vista of the city. After a while, Noctis asked:","“So what am I supposed to do?\"","Shadow raised an eyebrow.","\"What do you want to do?\"","The young man laughed, his voice entirely devoid of joy.","“Would I be asking if I knew the answer?\"","Shadow remained silent for a moment, then shrugged.","\"Well, I'd say you have three options. You can either help Arelen kill Irian, help Irian kill Arelen, or do nothing.”","He scratched the back of his head and then added with a hint of enthusiasm in his voice:","“Actually, there's a fourth option. You can kill both Arelen and Irian. That would be fair for everyone, wouldn't it?\"","Noctis stared at Shadow for a while. Eventually, he turned to look at Snuggle and shook his head.","\"Do me a favor, Snuggle. Remind me never to ask that guy for advice again...\""]},{"number":3203,"title":"Chapter 3203 Ultima Ratio Regum","paragraphs":["In the evening, Noctis was full of dismay and anger.","By the morning, he was in a low and somber mood, savoring tea in the courtyard of the inn with a distant expression on his face. Snuggle was keeping him company, hidden from sight in the draping of his colorful robe — the little doll did not say anything, so Shadow was not sure what her purpose in staying with the youth was.","It was a bit unfamiliar not to feel her tiny weight in his pocket, though... not that he minded.","Surely, he did not mind one bit.","In any case, Shadow had a lot to think about, as well. The conversation with the Altar Sage had stirred his memories, and those memories refused to leave him be. ‘Who doesn't want to be immortal?’ Shadow smiled bitterly.","Among his countless lives, there were some that had been cursed to last forever — even if none did, in the end.","He remembered being a prisoner of the Eternal City, his youthful and flawlessly healthy body infected by the virulent plague of a dead heretic's flesh. Thousands of years of torment, an eternity spent in the darkness of abyssal depths... the pain, the horror, the madness, the collapse of both his spirit and his mind.","He remembered being a Saint whose immortal body became a host for a terrifying vine. That eternity was no less traumatic to recall.","He remembered a shattered skeleton slowly crawling across a sea of obsidian dunes, denied the peaceful embrace of death even after coming uninvited to death's lightless realm.","No matter what kind of immortality Shadow could remember, it was always a curse. And how could it not be?","Death was peace, after all. Death was solace. Those who were refused its grace were doomed to never find either one. Shadow thought about his own endless and unforgiving existence. Wasn't he immortal already? If there was one thing that wielded no power over him, it was time.","However, he was not entirely immune to time, either.","Shadow would not be destroyed by its passage... but he was changing.","He was changing swiftly, in fact.","That was something he had noticed after entering the human city. Ever since meeting Snuggle, and then Noctis... ever since embarking on this misguided journey... he could not quite recognize himself.","Would the Shadow from the past have bothered to hide his identity? To get involved in the tiresome conflict of Transcendent rulers? To explain their schemes to a brash youth, let alone attempt to give that youth advice?","No. The creature Shadow had been would have never come to Arelen’s city, and even if he did, it would not have given that human any time.","But now that Shadow was surrounded by people, exposed to the bright radiance of day, the outer layers of his vast being were dissipating one after another.","What would be revealed when enough of them were gone?","He did not know, and was wary of finding out.","So even if Shadow did not care what would happen to these two Transcendent rulers and their lands, he found himself feeling troubled — no different from Noctis.","It was just that Shadow did not have to do anything, while Noctis had to do a lot.","He had to grow up, come to terms with the nuanced nature of the world, and make a difficult choice — all in the span of several days.","On the first day, Noctis remained in the courtyard of the inn, staring into the distance.","On the second day, he went outside, wandering the streets of the city and looking at the frightened refugees sheltered behind its walls.","On the third day, Noctis wanted to visit the stronghold and confront the Altar Sage... But before he could, war horns bellowed from beyond the city wall, causing a panic among the citizens.","Irian the Blade of Dawn had arrived at the head of her army.","“Damn it! Damn it! Damn it!\"","Cursing loudly, Noctis hurriedly put on his outer robes. He even layered colors that weren't complementary, which revealed just how great the turmoil in his heart was.","Observing him, Shadow raised an eyebrow.","\"So? Did you decide what to do?\"","He was genuinely curious what the youth would choose.","Noctis stared at him for a moment, then cursed under his breath and rushed outside.","\"No!\"","That was a kind of choice, as well. Opening the gates of the inn, Noctis threw a look over his shoulder and added:","\"Let's go take a look first. We can come up with something later.\"","Shadow lingered for a moment, then shrugged and followed. As he did, a squeaky voice resounded from somewhere down below.","“Wait for me! Wait for me!\"","Scurrying across the floorboards, Snuggle jumped clumsily, clutched the hem of his tunic, and climbed up to sit on his shoulder.","There, she huffed while catching her breath — which amused Shadow quite a lot, considering that the little doll did not need to breathe — and pointed forward.","“Let's go! Advance!\"","Shadow sighed.","Feeling like a giant who had been turned into a horse by a tiny human, he caught up with Noctis and pulled him into the shadows. A moment later, the three of them appeared on the battlements atop the wall. Arelen's soldiers were already there, hastily preparing for battle, and the Altar Sage himself had just arrived as well. He stood on the ramparts above the city gates, looking at the plain beyond with a composed expression. Winds tussled his auburn hair, and his eyes glistened in the golden light of dawn.","Out there on the field in front of the city, the enemy army had already assembled its ranks. Irian's warriors were far more numerous than the defenders of the city, and looked more seasoned as well.","As for their commander...","While Arelen had the air of a scholar, Irian the Blade of Dawn looked like a sharp weapon forged to cut down enemies on the battlefield.","She was a radiantly beautiful woman of tall stature, lithe and slender like a drawn sword, wearing armor crafted from white scales and polished bronze. In the rays of the rising sun, the bronze elements of her armor blazed with fiery radiance, as did the head of her long spear.","Dismounting from her snow-white warhorse, Irian raised her head and gazed at the gates of the city. Her hazel eyes were like liquid gold, and her hair was like a waterfall of warm sunlight, gathered into a braid and held in place by a bronze diadem.","“Arelen!\"","Her voice boomed above the vast field, making the soldiers on the wall tremble.","“I've come to seek justice for the lives of the innocent people you slew!\"","Pointing her long spear at the figure of the Altar Sage, Irian gritted her teeth and then shouted:","\"Come down and face me, coward! I'll send them off to the Shadow Realm by spilling your blood!\"","Arelen studied her silently from the battlements, then smiled.","“Innocent people? Those people were thieves who took that which did not belong to them. Surely, you did not bring your army here because I punished some thieves? Oh, but it looks like you did.\"","His smile turned cold and merciless.","“If so, why don't you come up and face me here instead?\"","Irian glared at him for a moment, then laughed darkly.","“So this is how it is. It seems that you have lost all your shame, Arelen the Altar Sage! Fine, then... let us end this dispute with sharp blades instead of treacherous words. Let us show the gods which one of us deserves to be the last one standing!\"","Atop the wall, Noctis clenched his fists.","“These two fools... why are they acting as if lam not even here?\"","Shadow shook his head lightly.","\"Oh, quite the opposite. They are both painfully aware of you. Irian is putting on a brave face, while Arelen is using the fact that you're on this side of the wall to rattle her.\"","A disbelieving chuckle escaped from the young hero's lips.","“Wonderful... simply wonderful. So even by doing nothing, I am still being used to bolster one side.\"","He smiled bitterly and shook his head.","“Ah... when I left the temple, I thought that if I was strong enough, valiant enough, and lucky enough, no enemy would be able to stand in my way. But these few days have taught me a bitter lesson, Shadow. Being strong and brave is great, sure.\"","His smile became a little mocking, as if he was ashamed of himself.","“But being cunning and devious is far more important. Who knew that sages would be deadlier than warriors? Alas, the word is truly mightier than the sword.\"","Shadow gave him a look of confusion.","“Well, of course it is. After all, any decent Shaper can turn a swordsman into a bloodstain by simply opening their mouth.\"","Looking the young Transcendent up and down, he sighed.","“It seems to me that you have chosen the fourth option? You are going to fight Arelen and Irian both?\"","Noctis smiled crookedly.","“What's the point? What will happen if I kill both of them? Nothing good...\"","He remained silent for a moment, then shook his head with a wistful expression.","“I can't do anything to resolve this situation. The best thing I can do... is do nothing.\"","Then, he turned and looked Shadow directly in the eye.","For a moment, a hint of hope flashed in his eyes.","“What about you, Shadow? Can you do something?\"","Sitting on Shadow's shoulder, Snuggle threw a nervous glance at him.","\"No, no... he can't. He promised not to kill anyone!\"","Shadow remained silent, looking at Irian's army with a calm expression.","Could he do something?","And if he could, was there a reason to be involved?","Troubled, Shadow looked down.","Slowly, a strange pain permeated his entire being, forcing him to give Noctis an answer. Finally, he sighed.","\"Can I? I guess I can.\"","On the walls of the city, the archers were nocking arrows on the strings of their bows.","Below the walls, on the field, Irian's army was preparing to charge.","The two Transcendents, former comrades, studied each other somberly. They were ready to clash and kill each other, as well. Mere moments remained until the start of the battle.","But before the first arrow pierced the radiance of dawn...","A dreadful roar suddenly split the heavens apart.","The ground quaked, and a cold wind blew","across the battlefield, causing deathly fear to grasp the hearts of mortal warriors with icy claws.","Something far more terrifying than either of the Transcendent rulers was approaching."]},{"number":3204,"title":"Chapter 3204 Hidden Menace","paragraphs":["The ground shook, and as a terrifying roar thundered above the two armies, dust spilled from between the great stone blocks that formed the wall. Atop the battlements, many of the soldiers lost their balance and fell, dropping their weapons. Below, on the battlefield, the horses of Irian's cavalry buckled in fear, making the riders curse as they struggled to remain in the saddle.","The infantrymen gripped their weapons, looking around with startled and frightened expressions.","Only a few people remained calm and collected, but even their expressions turned grim.","The Altar Sage, the Blade of Dawn, and the Beast of Twilight — the three Transcendent heroes glanced around, momentarily forgetting about their conflict.","\"W—what the hell?\"","Noctis peered into the distance, where a gargantuan hill was slowly crumbling. His voice sounded subdued.","Shadow, meanwhile, was leaning leisurely on the wall of a guard tower, his expression just as calm as it had always been.","He shrugged lightly.","“Who knows?\"","Irian and Arelen, meanwhile, were observing the calamity with wary gazes. Then, briefly, they glanced at each other. Far away, the hill had collapsed entirely, and something gargantuan, hideous, and malevolent moved slowly in the billowing cloud of dust. Suddenly, the radiant light of dawn grew pale and feeble, and the warmth of early summer turned into a piercing chill...","As though death itself had come to reap the two armies.","A moment later, the soldiers paled and staggered, some of them even fainting — that was because the overwhelming presence of the hidden menace washed over them, followed by the suffocating pressure of a vast and alien Will.","Sitting on Shadow's shoulder, Snuggle turned her head to look at him, then stood up slowly and pulled on his hair.","Her squeaky voice was reduced to a barely audible whisper:","“H—hey! Are you not... overdoing it a little?\"","Shadow just smiled faintly.","“Am I? It depends on how strong these mortal heroes are, I suppose.\"","He spoke quietly enough for Noctis not to hear — the young Transcendent was not listening to Shadow, anyway, his entire attention focused on the immense figure moving slowly under the veil of dust. Finally, the Altar Sage uttered a Verse, and a powerful gale tore apart the cloud of dust, revealing the true form of the unknown creature.","Standing atop the wall, he was the first to behold it. His face paled, and his gaze turned grim.","Out there on the plain in front of the city, a towering abomination was slowly crawling out of the shattered earth. Its body was long and segmented, like that of a centipede, but its head resembled a giant human skull that was missing the lower jaw, with three empty eye sockets that hid impenetrable darkness.","The chitinous carapace of the giant abomination was so black that it seemed to absorb the surrounding light. The enormous skull, however, was vibrantly scarlet, as if it had been bathed in an ocean of human blood until the surface of the ancient bone fully absorbed it.","Finally climbing from the depths of earth, the hideous centipede raised its long neck. Even with most of its body still on the ground, the scarlet skull loomed at least a hundred meters above it, turned in the direction of the city.","The three empty eye sockets of the titanic abomination stared at the three Transcendent heroes, eerily emotionless, the unfathomable pools of darkness hidden within them still and hollow.","What was not still, however, were hundreds of ghastly maws that revealed themselves on the inner side of the creature's belly, gnashing myriads of teeth as they revealed the crimson flesh of the monster. Witnessing the great immensity of the abhorrent creature, the soldiers of Irian's army, who stood between the city and the subterranean horror, took an unconscious step back — in the direction of the wall they had been meant to besiege.","Irian herself seemed rattled, as well. Looking at the eerie scarlet skull, she gripped her spear and whispered in a stunned voice:","\"A Great Monster!\"","She could not see the soul of the giant creature, of course. But merely by sensing the oppressive power of its presence, as well as the malevolent flavor of its Will, she could make a judgment.","Atop the wall, Arelen wore a grave expression, as well.","Noctis, meanwhile...","Seemed thoroughly appalled.","“A centipede! Ah, eww! Why did it have to be a damn centipede?! I hate them!\"","He shuddered, grimacing in utter disgust. Shadow spared him an amused look.","“That's what you worried about?\"","He was a little bit hurt.","After all, he had gone into a lot of trouble to create that monster.","The giant Nightmare Creature was not an Nightmare Creature at all. Instead, it was merely a construct woven out of manifested shadows, controlled by his will. Its flesh was equal in toughness to that of a Supreme being, since it was infused with his Supreme essence.","As for the power of its presence and the malevolence of its Will, those were simply the presence and Will of Shadow — a sliver of them, at least — which he revealed when the monster appeared.","Creating such a monstrosity was no easy feat, but not that difficult either. Its carapace, its muscles, its tendons, its fangs, and all the other parts of its enormous body — Shadow manifested them all and then connected them together into a functional organism, breathing a false spark of life into that organism with his nuanced control.","He had even gone into the trouble of changing the color of its bones and its flesh, thinking that showing a creature painted entirely black would put Noctis into a difficult position. The youth had just returned from supposedly vanquishing an unknown horror that dwelled in eternal darkness, after all, so Shadow didn't want anyone to think that the monster followed the Beast of Twilight to this peaceful city from a distant realm.","As for whether Irian and Arelen would believe that the giant centipede was indeed a Creature of Corruption... Shadow did not particularly care. Unlike soul essence, his own was the essence of shadows — so, even if they had means of peering into the souls of living beings, they would not see the familiar silver radiance.","And even if they discerned that something was not quite right, it did not matter. The nature of the monster was not as important as its perceived malice and intent to destroy the city.","\"Irian!\"","Standing atop the wall, Arelen shouted his adversary's name. The radiant Transcendent who had come to kill him glanced up, and the two seemed to converse silently, their gazes full of concerned wariness.","Then, after exchanging a nod, they both rushed toward the towering creature side by side.","Noctis cursed and leaped down from the wall, as well, dashing to follow them. Moments later, Shadow and Snuggle were left alone among terrified soldiers.","\"What the hell did you create, Shadow?\"","Snuggle's voice sounded oddly weak. Looking down at her in surprise, Shadow raised an eyebrow.","“What? It's merely a construct.\"","He paused for a moment, then added with a shrug:","“Actually, I didn't even have to work that hard on it. That thing was already something I had considered creating — back when I was thinking of making a better vessel for you. A battle golem, of sorts.\"","The little doll trembled and stared at him in dismay.","“T—that? You wanted me — me! — to climb inside that thing? That disgusting, ghastly thing over there?!\"","Shadow looked at her in confusion.","“Why? Look at it. It's very sturdy, can move below and above ground really fast, and has a lot of ways to kill enemies. And it is very menacing — instilling the adversary with fear is half the victory, you know.\"","He scratched the tip of his nose awkwardly.","“Admittedly, it can't fly. Adding a sufficient number of wings introduced too many points of vulnerability to the carapace, so I was left with no choice but to scrap that idea. Still. I think it turned out pretty well.\"","He smiled proudly.","\"I call it... the Giant Red Skull Centipede, Prototype One.\"","Snuggle groaned and covered her face with a hand.","“Prototype One, he says... gods have mercy, look how proud he is! He's completely serious, too!\"","Shadow blinked a couple of times.","\"It's a fitting name, though? I don't see the issue.\"","Perhaps Snuggle was simply too young to appreciate his stellar namingship.","Well... what else would one expect from a doll called Snuggle?","Far in the distance, the giant monster lowered its head and flowed forward like a river of scarlet darkness, moving toward the three Transcendent heroes with terrifying speed, the ground turning into a shredded mess of torn soil and seething mucus wherever it passed.","Shadow sighed.","‘All that work, only for it to be destroyed...’","Even though he had promised Snuggle not to kill anyone and created this construct specifically to be slain by the mortal heroes... he still found himself secretly rooting for the giant centipede.","After all, if its own creator couldn't support this soulless construct, wouldn't it be just too pitiful?","A split second later, on the plain in front of the city, three Transcendent heroes — Arelen the Altar Sage, Irian the Blade of Dawn, and Noctis, the Crimson Beast of Twilight — clashed with the harrowing Nightmare Creature... Giant Red Skull Centipede, Prototype One.","Their battle would become a legend all across the mortal realms in the future, one day soon."]},{"number":3205,"title":"Chapter 3205 Three Heroes Faced a Dreadful Worm","paragraphs":["\"No, no! You are telling it wrong, blind fool! You weren't even there, so what do you know? But I! I saw it all! I was standing atop the wall when the three heroes faced the dreadful beast of the Underworld, the ghastly spawn of appalling Corruption, the great and grotesque Nightmare Creature, devourer of human souls... the Giant Red Skull Centipede!\"","The streets of the city were lively today.","In the early morning, when Shadow and Noctis stopped to enjoy one last cup of tea before leaving the city to resume their journey, they had no choice but to hear people retelling the story of the recent battle.","Despite being praised as a valiant hero, Noctis wore a sullen expression. Cursing quietly, he threw a resentful glance at Shadow, then raised his cup and used the wide sleeves of his colorful robe to hide his face.","Shadow smiled faintly.","The soldier, meanwhile, continued his story.","\"Hear, hear! There I was, standing atop the wall and drawing the string of my bow when the ground shook, and a ghostly chill permeated the air. The soldiers of Lady Irian's army below the wall all scattered and fell, their horses foaming at the mouth and going mad from terror. At that moment, all of us felt the icy breath of Death, and our limbs grew weak and feeble. Only three courageous heroes endured it — our wise ruler, Arelen the Altar Sage, the brave and radiant Lady Irian, the Blade of Dawn, and young Noctis, Child of the Moon... the Beast of Twilight!\"","Shadow looked at Noctis and said in a low tone:","“Did you hear? He's talking about you, Child of the Moon!\"","Noctis lowered his head and groaned.","“What was that? I didn't hear anything!\"","Shadow chuckled.","The soldier slammed his cup, sending drops of tea flying into the air, and glanced around with wide eyes.","\"And there, in the distance, was the Great Creature of Corruption — the ancient horror who crawls below the world, the corpse eater, the guardian of the Abyss. The Giant Red Skull Centipede! Surely, you must have heard of the infamous calamities it had caused throughout the ages!\"","A few of the listeners nodded hesitantly, their faces pale.","“Right... right. Giant Red Skull Centipede? Of course, I heard of it! I am not some ignorant fool, after all. Isn't it... uh... isn't it that thing Heart God once cast into the abyss after it gnawed on the insides of the Heart Tree's fruit?\"","“No, you're thinking of the Spirit Worm, Abundance! The Giant Red Skull Centipede is a different worm; it's the corpse worm that devoured the flesh of Beast God's first avatar!\"","“That's right! Not only that, but I also heard that it was the bane of First Humans. White Abyss herself had once battled the Giant Red Skull Centipede, but the creature's profane carapace could not be burned even by her flames!\"","“Goodness... such a terrifying Nightmare Creature...\"","\"To think that it actually burrowed under our city. Gods, I am still trembling!\"","The soldier glanced at his listeners with scorn.","\"Indeed! That is how dreadful that Nightmare Creature was. I saw it with my own two eyes — as long as a mountain chain, its head reaching the heavens... no, not simply reaching the heavens! It was so enormous that clouds were like its crown, surrounding the scarlet skull and spilling out of its terrifying eye sockets. It had a myriad of bloody maws! Ten myriads of dreadful legs! When it moved, it was as if the rivers of the Underworld spilled from the depths of earth, consuming the world like a tide of darkness!\"","He took a deep breath.","“All of us were ready to leave for the Shadow Realm... except for the three heroes. Undaunted by the ghastly visage of the ancient curse, they rushed across the plain to meet it. Ah, the sight of them! The majesty of the Altar Sage, the breathtaking radiance of the Blade of Dawn, the thoughtless brashness of the Beast of Twilight...\"","Noctis turned his head and hissed through gritted teeth.","“Did he just call me a thoughtless bastard?!\"","Shadow gestured for him to calm down.","“He did not. And keep your voice down.\"","They were sitting in a corner, far from the gathered crowd. However, drawing attention would still be troublesome.","From Shadow's pocket, Snuggle squeaked quietly:","\"Even if he did, so what?!\"","Noctis hid his face, while the soldier continued:","“When the three heroes clashed with the monstrous Nightmare Creature... the sky quaked! The ground shattered! The winds screamed in agony, and the fierce thunder of that terrifying clash echoed across all mortal realms, reaching even the blessed reaches of the six Divine abodes. Lady Irian struck first, her spear shining like a ray of sunlight... but, alas! Oh, woe! The creature's carapace, forged from adamantine darkness, was too tough to be pierced! With not even a scratch left on it...\"","The tale continued in the same manner.","“And that was when our wise lord assumed his Transcendent form, his wings reaching toward the heavens. His talons sank into the cracks between the plates of the Nightmare Creature’s armor, and his beak fell upon the scarlet skull as a hammer falls on an anvil, like an owl snatching a snake from tall grass...\"","\"The Nightmare Creature bellowed then, its voice scattering all hope! Not even valiant Lady Irian could withstand the ghastly power of that call, falling to one knee and spitting a mouthful of blood. Each drop was like a precious ruby, and her porcelain face turned to pure alabaster, making it even more tantalizing...\"","“And it was then! When all hope seemed to be lost! That the Crimson Beast of Twilight rushed forward like a torrent of pale moonlight, like a ghostly wolf woven out of bravery and bloodlust, his vicious fangs sinking into the black carapace of the ancient horror. He tore at the creature with his claws, shredding its neck in his jaws, completely fearless!\"","Eventually, the soldier ran out of breath. As his listeners leaned forward, he gulped down his tea and let out a long sigh.","“And that was how the three mortal heroes slew a monster as old as the gods themselves! The Altar Sage held its skull in place, the Beast of Twilight tore apart its neck, and the Blade of Dawn delivered the decisive blow, severing the skull from the Nightmare Creature’s endless body. The Giant Red Skull Centipede writhed then, hills and forests perishing in the violence of its death throes. By luck, the warriors of Lady Irian's army had retreated to the city wall by then — if not, all of them would have perished, as well.\"","He shuddered.","\"And once the Nightmare Creature lost its life, its body turned into a tide of darkness, flowing back into the depths of earth — not even the ghastly skull remained. All that remained were two enormous soul shards. Our lord took one, while Lady Irian took the other — young Noctis, meanwhile, being a humble and modest youth, simply bowed to his elders, saying that protecting humans from the horrors of Corruption was already a worthy reward.\"","A lone tear rolled down the soldier's weathered face.","“Such virtue!\"","The soldier's tale was quite engaging. In fact, similar stories were being told all around the city at the moment — wandering rhapsodes were already writing songs about the battle, each competing in who could exaggerate it more.","Noctis, however, gnashed his teeth.","\"Says who?! I wanted a soul shard, too! They just snatched them first!\"","Shadow glanced at him and raised an eyebrow.","“You want one? There's plenty more where those two came from. I can donate a couple more.\"","The soul shards had come from the depths of his soul, where he had stored them centuries ago. All kinds of creatures had visited his kingdom over the ages, and after killing them, Shadow had little use for their soul shards — so he had quite a few by now. Noctis stared at him for a moment, then shook his head.","\"You took all the fun out of it, so what's the point?\"","The soldier was still talking, but there was no point in listening anymore — not that there had been.","In truth, the three Transcendents had barely managed to destroy the Giant Red Skull Centipeded, Prototype One. Shadow had even considered giving in a little, but luckily, Noctis stepped up at that moment and helped them bring the construct down. All three heroes were severely wounded during the battle, though, having barely survived — that was fortunate, at least. After dealing with the Great Monster, Arelen and Irian were in no mood to fight each other. So, in a peculiar turn of events, the besieging army ended up camping under the city wall, with some soldiers even entering the city to purchase supplies and receive medical attention.","The war was over... for now, at least.","Noctis sighed.","“You could have warned me, you know! I was so proud of myself... until Snuggle informed me that the supposed Great Monster was not a Creature of Corruption at all, and instead a puppet you created out of boredom.\"","He shivered and gave Shadow an uneasy look.","“By the way, Shadow... forgive me for saying this. But you're a sick bastard. That thing you made was so abhorrent! What kind of troubled mind can even come up with something like this?!\"","Shadow contemplated the answer for a moment.","“I'm pretty healthy, I think?\"","Noctis let out a disbelieving laugh, then shook his head and shivered once more.","“By the moon... if this is what he makes when he's bored, I'm scared to imagine what he'll do if something actually angers him.\"","He remained silent for a short while, then asked.","\"I still don't get it, though. After the battle, both Irian and Arelen were severely weakened. Wasn't it a perfect moment to stab each other in the back? But they suddenly seem nice and friendly again. In fact, it's like nothing happened — as if they weren't at each other's throats just a few days ago.\"","Shadow shrugged.","\"That's to be expected. You really don't understand why? It's very simple.\"","He poured himself more tea.","“Ambition, aspiration... powerlust, greed... loyalty to one's subject and the desire to leave your mark upon the world, to conquer the heavens. All of those are powerful motivations, but there is one thing that trumps them all. Do you know what it is?\"","Noctis slowly shook his head.","In response, Shadow just smiled faintly.","“It's fear. Irian and Arelen have forgotten fear, but I reminded them. I showed them that, in this world, there is no safety. There is no assurance. Even if you spend your entire life cleansing your lands of abominations, one day, a horror that you cannot defeat alone can just pop up from underground and swallow your city whole.\"","He sighed and then added, feeling a strange melancholy:","“After all, no one survives in this world alone.”","Shadow chuckled.","\"So, in a sense... even if all else fails to bring peace, fear can.\"","Noctis stared at him silently for a while, then asked in a subdued tone:","“So you think that there will really be peace in this land now?\"","Shadow lingered a little, then slowly shook his head.","\"There will be... for a while. But in the end, war will come to replace it again.\"","He finished his tea and rose, ready to leave the tavern — and the city — behind him.","“In the end, Arelen was right. This land will only know true peace when there's only one power left to rule it.”","With that, he turned around and headed away.","Noctis grimaced, then followed him.","\"I think you're wrong, though.\"","He smiled.","“There are six gods, after all, and they don't often quarrel. There are even other deities —a throng of Spirits, even the daemons. And the heavens are not consumed by war, are they?\"","The Shadow glanced ahead, his expression a little wistful.","\"Yeah. The heavens are at peace.\"","They were, for now.","Soon, the three of them left through the open gates of the city, passed the encampment of Irian's army, and headed away.","The city slowly disappeared from view. The road ahead was long.","Their journey was only just beginning, after all..."]},{"number":3206,"title":"Chapter 3206 Bad Weather","paragraphs":["People had always imagined hell as a place full of fire. But, as it turned out, hell was full of wind and water instead.","NQSC was swallowed by a storm. The sky was obscured by a dark, menacing veil of clouds, and hurricane winds howled as they tore through the crumbled remains of the city barriers and collapsed buildings in the outer rings of the city. Rain fell like a wall, flying sideways from the sheer force of the powerful gale. Flashes of lightning burned the darkness away, and deafening claps of thunder roared high above, as if there was a malevolent, hungry dragon hidden in the storm.","Storms like this one had been happening more and more often over the past four years, eventually fusing into a never-ending deluge of calamity.","Of course, despite all the damage caused by the unceasing natural catastrophes, it was merely a background for the true disaster.","The true disaster was the Nightmare Gates that now surrounded the city like siege towers and the endless swarms of abominations escaping them each day.","The world was truly and utterly ending.","In fact, it was already halfway gone.","It had started slowly, but then proceeded swiftly. There were simply more and more Nightmare Gates, more abominations, and more casualties among the soldiers who desperately protected Earth from being torn apart. Then, pieces of the waking world began fusing with the Dream Realm, adding their weight to its patchwork surface.","Once the two realms became partially fused, the Nightmare Creatures did not need Gates to travel between them anymore. That alone added immense pressure to the strained defenses of humanity, but there was even more damage. A planet was a closed and finely tuned system, after all. Once a hostile mystical realm started taking bites out of it, nature itself went insane, causing rapid and unpredictable changes.","Hence, the storms.","Here in NQSC, at least, it was mainly storms. Elsewhere, it was something else — volcanic eruptions, earthquakes, tsunamis, sharp temperature changes...","It was not all bad, though. Yes, the infusion of alien air had caused the sky above NQSC to go insane... but it was clean air. Even now that the air filtration barriers were breached or collapsed, people were not being poisoned on the street — in fact, they could breathe freely without face masks for the first time in hundreds of years.","Even the end of the world had its perks.","“Move aside, bastards! Let them through! As soon as the rear vehicle clears, close ranks!\"","“What are you doing, fool?! This guy is still alive! Drag him back and hand him over to the medics!\"","“Report! Left highrise turrets, ammunition spent!\"","“Sir! They're coming!\"","“Argh, curse it all! Anyone whose armor still has more than thirty percent charge left, advance to the front row!\"","“Best seats in the establishment! Let's enjoy the show, gentlemen!\"","“Light them up!\"","On a street between two battered dormitory towers, the joints of powered armor suits hissed as soldiers unleashed a hail of bullets and explosive rounds into the rushing tide of Nightmare Creatures. Behind them, towering MWPs charged their mass drivers, rising monstrous machine guns to bathe the abominations in lead and tungsten hail. The turrets above the highrises spun, spitting out long streams of tracer rounds.","The roaring salvo of countless shots drowned out the deafening blast of thunder... but it failed to drown out the chilling wails of the rushing Nightmare Creatures.","The soldiers of the first line of defense paled, preparing to deploy their bayonets.","\"I... I don't think I like this show, guys!\"","“Wow, really?! You don't say!\"","“It's about to end, though! At least for us!\"","\"What a silver lining!\"","The soldiers had been fighting the entire day, slowly retreating street by street as the civilians of the breached district were being evacuated deeper into the city. Now, however, it looked like for many of the soldiers, this was going to be the last stand.","Just before the tide of abominations overwhelmed the makeshift defensive position, a swift figure streaked through the air and plummeted into their mass.","“Brace for impact!\"","There was a muffled boom.","In the next moment, the entire center of the Nightmare Creature horde was pulverized, hundreds of them dying in an instant. It was difficult to see because of the torrential rain and furious wind, but countless abominations that were close to the figure simply turned into bloody mist, while those that had been further away were merely torn to tiny pieces.","Hide, chitin, flesh, bone — everything was crushed and ground to dust in a split second, as if struck by a celestial hammer, flung outward by a heavy shockwave.","A heartbeat later, lightning illuminated the world, and the startled soldiers saw a blurry streak moving through the swarm of Nightmare Creatures with astonishing speed. Wherever it passed, scores of abominations were severed, beheaded, and split open — as if the binds that held their bodies together were being undone.","One soldier, whose visual acuity was better than most, caught a glimpse of a great zweihander flashing in a magnificent arc.","\"It's... it's the Lady of Sorrow!\"","\"What?! Isn't she a Saint?!\"","“Since when is Lady Sorrow in NQSC?!\"","“A Saint has descended from the sky... now that's an ending!\"","“Stop staring and push forward, fools! Support the lady and her people!\"","“Left highrise turrets have finished the reloading sequence!\"","“The last convoy has entered the Barrier, sir!\"","\"Advance!\"","The situation on this battlefield had changed in an instant. Lady of Sorrow — Tamar of Clan Sorrow — was one of the youngest Saints of humanity, having conquered her Third Nightmare only recently. However, her fame had been steadily spreading among people even before that, when she was a mere Master. Most of the renowned figures of humanity were affiliated with one of the great powers in one way or another. There were Saints serving one of the two queens, Morgan of Valor or Song Seishan, and those who served Nightwalker and the House of Night. There were some who followed Ananke of Weave or one of the three Supreme protectors of the waking world.","Tamar of Sorrow and her small band of elite warriors, however, were one of the few independent forces that roamed the realms while serving no one. Nobody ever knew where they would pop up, which battlefield she would grace with her presence... wherever it was, however, countless Nightmare Creatures died, and tides of battle were usually reversed.","Invigorated, the soldiers pushed forward, aiming to eliminate the remaining abominations before organizing an orderly retreat.","Tamar, meanwhile, cleaved far into the crumbling horde, moving deeper and deeper like a whirlwind of blood and steel.","[Don't get too excited. Pull back.]","The voice came from a Memory used by members of the Shadow Clan — with this many Gates, technology became more and more unreliable, causing a crisis of command and communication among the soldiers of humanity. Where technology failed, sorcery and Awakened picked up the slack.","In that regard, the Shadow Clan was better off than any other faction.","Tamar smiled grimly.","[Who says that I am excited?]","Finally, she reached the Tyrant who controlled the horde from the rear. Leaping into the air, she stepped on it to change her trajectory and avoid a deadly blow, then did it again to launch herself toward the creature's massive head.","[I am exhausted. I want to lie down. I want to take a hot shower. I want to eat something warm, too...]","The creature's head split apart, a fountain of fetid blood mixing with the falling rain. Tamar landed on the wet asphalt, slid a few dozen meters, and brought herself to a halt by transforming her momentum into a blast of concussive force that tore a hole in the nearest abomination.","[Most of all, I want to get somewhere dry. Damn rain...]","Her Memory spoke again:","[Hey. That was uncalled for.]","In that moment, a powerful gust of wind slammed into Tamar, obscuring her vision with a veil of water.","Half-blinded, she looked around.","‘It is time to pull back, indeed.'","She had performed well in front of the soldiers, but in truth, she was not in good shape. Beneath the armor, her body was bruised and battered, littered with wounds — and beneath them, there were the wounds from the previous battlefield that had been treated, but had not healed fully yet.","Things had been getting worse and worse as of late, and there was no respite in sight. Antarctica had fallen first. By now, it was most likely fully absorbed by the Dream Realm, most of it transported to somewhere beyond the Burned Forest. As such, it had become an open wound in the flesh of Earth, unleashing an endless flood of Nightmare Creatures — that alone would have been enough to overwhelm the remaining Quadrants... if not for Revel and the Shadow Clan.","Somewhere out there, on the unknown northern front of apocalypse, Saint Revel was leading the forces of the Shadow Clan, including the powerful Shadows and the legion of shades their boss had left in her care, against the Barrow Wraiths and countless abominations of the Burned Forest. In fact, she had staged a counteroffensive and invaded the charred Death Zone a couple of years ago.","Because of Revel pulling the attention of all those Nightmare Creatures to the Forgotten Shore, fewer of them were spilling into the waking world.","Still... their number was enough to make the oceans of Earth completely inaccessible. Navigating them had always been perilous, but now, it was pure suicide. Even Saints did not dare to traverse the oceans.","The colonies in South America had been evacuated, but the three remaining Quadrants were completely isolated from each other now. With global infrastructure in tatters, famine had long become a real possibility — even with most population centers possessing robust food self-sustenance systems, those had long been cripplied by the spreading influence of the Call.","In the end, the only thing that was preventing humanity from starving was the Night Garden and its captain, who could both carry people from the waking world to the Dream Realm and bring food from the Dream Realm to the waking world on the way back. Raised by Wolves could help, as well.","It was quite ironic... before, people of the Dream Realm staved off starvation with supplies from Earth, But now, the situation was entirely reversed.","Which was not to say that the people in the Dream Realm knew no hunger. The more the situation in the waking world worsened, the more refugees poured into the human enclaves there. By now, a good one-third of humanity had left its cradle, pushing the population of the Dream Realm well beyond one billion.","And the Dream Realm... the Dream Realm was in no way ready to accept this many people.","Things weren't going well there either, after all.","On Earth, the three remaining Quadrants were under a constant siege, both from beyond and from within. In the Dream Realm, meanwhile, the same was true for the three Domains — even with the Sovereigns leading the battle, humanity was struggling to hold on to its land.","Expanding their reach, of course, had become completely impossible.","The wilderness was too dangerous, and the Citadel Cities weren't made of rubber. By now, every single one of them was overpopulated and suffering from resource shortages.","A few had already been lost.","'We are not dead yet.'","Tamar looked at the ravaged urban landscape in front of her with a grim expression.","They were not dead... but they were certainly dying.","Humanity was like a wounded soldier slowly bleeding out on the ground, hoping that a medic would arrive in time to save them.","It was only that the medics who could save humanity were stuck in a Nightmare.","They had been gone for four years already, and nobody knew when they would come back."]},{"number":3207,"title":"Chapter 3207 The Apocalypse Happened Yesterday","paragraphs":["As Tamar retreated, nimbly dashing through the air when towering carcasses blocked her way, the remains of the horde tried to pursue her. Whenever a Nightmare Creature got too close, a black arrow fell from above, its passage almost invisible in the stormy darkness. The arrows struck the abominations unerringly, pinning them down — however, not a single creature died.","Thinking that Rain was enduring the storm somewhere on the roof made Tamar feel better. After all, there was nothing more sad than being miserable alone... being miserable together with a friend was much better.","‘Damn storm...’","The battle for NQSC had been long and gruelling, but for Tamar, the constant rain and unceasing wind felt more exhausting than endless waves of Nightmare Creatures — which was a bit peculiar, considering that her ancestral Citadel used to stand atop the Weeping Goddess.","Until the King of Nothing destroyed it.","Who would have guessed that she'd be praying for his return one day?","His and that of her boss, of course, as well as the other two Supremes who had challenged the Fifth Nightmare.","[I'm retreating.]","The soldiers almost reached the Barrier. Their retreat was orderly, but just to be safe, the Shadow Clan agents under Tamar's command were covering it. Now, it was time for them to escape as well.","‘How many hours can we rest?'","Revel was in the Dream Realm, tied in a vicious war against the Barrow Wraiths and the horrors of the Burned Forest... for now. Last Tamar heard, something was stirring in the rotten corpse of the dead World Tree — so it was unclear how long the Lightslayer would be able to hold on.","That battlefield was too deadly for most human members of the Shadow Clan, though. So, most of them had been sent to various flashpoints of the apocalypse both in the Dream Realm and on Earth, moving in the shadows and accomplishing tasks that demanded an elite force with a delicate touch.","That was how it had been in the beginning, at least... by now, many of them operated in the open, pretending to be independent Awakened — those who were still alive, of course. Tamar had conquered her Third Nightmare recently and was hurriedly sent to the Northern Quadrant, where Rain was in command.","Despite still being a Master, the Princess of Shadows had become somewhat irreplaceable for their ragtag group of knaves and misfits. Her powers were simply too mystical, while her ability as a sorceress was second to none. So, no one was surprised that she was in charge of Saints despite being of a lower Rank, still.","By now, many of humanity's forces had been pulled to NQSC... but even with all of them fighting desperately to keep the city intact, the Nightmare Creatures were slowly pushing them back.","The outskirts had been swallowed almost a year ago. The outer barriers held out for many months, but were eventually breached and conquered by abominations. Now, the last district in the outer ring of the city was being abandoned... which meant that the defenders were fully retreating behind the Barrier.","The Barrier was something that Nightwalker had created. It was a zone surrounding the inner city where space was so torn and twisted that it had become a demented, deadly labyrinth — if one didn't have a special enchanted token, they could very well become lost there for the rest of their lives.","Or for eternity.","Nightmare Creatures still made their way through, but many of them perished or were weakened in the process. So, while the Barrier was not a panacea, it helped the defenders of the city keep at least the inner districts intact.","The battle for NQSC was tough...","But then again, it was tough everywhere. The entire population of the Eastern Quadrant was locked in a bloody war against the horrors that crawled onto the coast from the depths of the ocean. The Western Quadrant was already being consumed by the Dream Realm, and the situation there was even more desperate than here in the north.","Granted, there were relatively few people left there who had not been evacuated to the Dream Realm already — the Northern Quadrant was slowly and surely becoming the last bastion of humanity on Earth, as well as its final battlefield.","Out there in the Dream Realm, the situation was not much better. Its territory was shifting, new regions appearing in the middle of well-charted lands. As a result, old horrors that had been resting in their lairs for eons were stirring, directing their gazes at the human settlements.","The Stormsea was boiling and seething, rivers of blood flowing into its misty water. Silver Web was still holding, and the city in the delta of the River of Tears was holding as well — but they were under constant siege. The basin of the great river had become one vast battlefield, with isolated Citadel Cities barely holding the Nightmare Creatures at bay.","In the east, the eerie darkness had finally stopped spreading after swallowing half a dozen Citadels. However, nobody knew when it would start moving again. Ravenheart was being besieged by the snow wraiths of the frozen wastelands. Bastion was faring relatively well, but the connection to the northern territories had been cut...","And recently, waves of powerful Nightmare Creatures had begun to flow out from the belt of Death Zones lying between the Godgrave and the Stormsea. Morgan and her warriors took the brunt of that tide of horrors, even if some of it spilled into the basin of the River of Tears as well.","Morgan, Seishan, and Ananke... each of them had battled Cursed Nightmare Creatures in the past four years. For now, they were yet to be defeated, but each of those battles had left scars both on their bodies and on the surface of the Dream Realm itself.","The wardens of the waking world had fared somewhat better, but they were exhausted by the need to both fight endlessly and resist the hostile pressure of the very realm they were trying to protect. Still, their presence was like a ray of hope in the sea of nightmares — every time the soldiers of humanity witnessed Raised By Wolves, Nightingale, or Soul Reaper, their morale soared.","It was just that only one of them could be present in the waking world at a time — they had to take turns entering the battlefield, lest a dire crisis happened when none of them could return. And there were too many battlefields on Earth for one being to be enough, even if that being was Supreme.","\"Ready your tokens!\"","Tamar was the last to arrive in front of the Barrier, rushing ahead of the pursuing mob of Nightmare Creatures. Several cohorts of the Shadow Clan fighters were already waiting for her there, clad in sleek suits of black armor, armed with both Memories and mundane weapons. Rain had descended from the highrise as well, looking at the turrets the soldiers had to abandon with regret.","Tamar leaned on her zweihander, breathing heavily. All around her, her soldiers pulled the enchanted markers that would allow them to pass the Barrier from beneath their armor.","At that moment, blaring alarms roared all across the city.","Looking at her mechanical watch — a relic that had become priceless ever since humanity began to settle the Dream Realm while the Call began disrupting delicate electronics — she cursed.","‘Moonrise...’","Many terrifying things had happened when the boundary between the waking world and the Dream Realm began to become blurry, but none was more terrifying than what was happening to the Moon.","There had been a saying before that looking at the Moon too closely was perilous. Now, however, it was especially so — somewhere along the way, simply glancing up while the moon was visible in the sky became deadly. Many people had died, many had instantly gone mad, and even more of them had immediately become infected by Corruption.","Those who were mundane were dragged into the First Nightmare, most of them turning into abominations and slaughtering everyone around them. Those who were Awakened simply turned, to a much more devastating effect.","And with every month, the influence of the Moon was only growing more intense, frightening, and malevolent.","Tamar was a Saint, and the sky above NQSC was obscured by heavy clouds. Still, she lowered her gaze.","At that moment, another flash of lightning illuminated the word, and Rain pulled back the hood of her black raincoat to look up. Her expression did not seem good. Knowing that her friend often sensed things that other people couldn't, Tamar tensed.","\"What?\"","Rain hesitated for a moment, then gritted her teeth and pointed at the sky. Tamar hesitated, then glanced at the seething mass of storm clouds above them.","There, hidden by the hurricane, something gargantuan was moving between the bolts of lightning. In fact, it seemed as if the heavens had gone mad, attacking the titanic form in berserk fury. Dozens, then hundreds of twisting eclectic arcs struck the colossal shadow as it slowly revealed itself.","The brilliance of myriad bolts of lightning illuminated the world like a pale sun.","Tamar paled.","A moment later, the Night Garden revealed itself from the storm.","The great ship had descended below the stormclouds, revealing its battered form to the people sheltered in the city. Its size was so immense that it was difficult to fathom, wreathed in lightning and glowing with residual energy.","And, at the moment, another form — one infinitely vast, grotesque, and repulsive — was wrapped around the ship's hull, straining to crush it.","Tamar couldn't see the upper part of the giant Nightmare Creature, but each of its tattered wings was large enough to cover an entire district of the city. One was severed and charred; the other was clawing at the Mainmast Pagoda of the living ship with giant, curving talons.","Myriad arrows streaked from the deck of the Night Garden to pierce its body, and enormous cannons roared one after another, each taking out huge chunks of flesh from its belly. An enormous figure woven out of starlight was rending the creature's back... but even with all these efforts, it didn't seem to be on the threshold of death yet.","Tamar took an involuntary step back.","\"What... what the hell is this?\"","A Titan? A Cursed Nightmare Creature?","\"We need to get behind the Barrier.\"","Rain's voice sounded calm, but Tamar knew her well enough to recognize an underlying layer of trepidation.","She glanced at her friend with a silent question.","Rain pulled the barrier token out and turned back.","\"It's falling. It's going to impact somewhere beyond the city... but close. So, we need to run. What are you standing around for, guys?! Run, run, run!\"","Throwing one last look at the Night Garden, Tamar gritted her teeth and dove into the Barrier.","Behind her, Nightmare Creatures were flooding the ravaged street like a grotesque river.","A bolt of lightning flashed, and a deafening thunderclap shook the world.","Another day of the apocalypse was coming to an end."]},{"number":3208,"title":"Chapter 3208 Out of the Frying Pan","paragraphs":["‘Curse it all!'","As the wind howled and the endless bolts of lightning scorched the sky, a ferocious mass of dark clouds churning like a celestial ocean, the Night Garden plummeted toward the ground. At first, Nightwalker simply meant to descend below the clouds to shield his warriors from the rising moon — but now, the living ship was wounded too severely to be controlled, and its fall had become unstoppable.","Of course, the titanic creature holding it in a crushing grip was not helping the situation either.","The hull of the great vessel was slowly devouring its flesh, but the damn abomination was too vast and too powerful — there were fractures slowly appearing on the miraculous wood already, and the damage being dealt to the Night Garden was far beyond what the living ship could return.","Usually, slamming into the ground would not have been a major concern. However, with the ship already damaged, a collision could very well become catastrophic — not to mention that the impact would devastate countless districts of NQSC.","The Night Garden was a dozen kilometers from stern to bow, after all, and its mass was incalculable. The speed of its fall looked deceptively tame because of its size, but in truth, it was dire.","Nightwalker couldn't right the ship with the damn Titan weighing it down, though. Sinking his colossal, ethereal fangs into the flesh of the monster, he tore off an enormous chunk of flesh and bellowed, his eerie voice drowning out the deafening roars of the storm.","His Transcendent form, the Starbeast, was uncanny and immensely powerful. However, one thing it did not possess was vocal cords capable of human speech... it was alright, though. Because Aether could understand him.","So, what Nightwalker was relaying to his warriors was quite simple:","“Aether! Concentrate on its right shoulder joint! Take its remaining wing off!\"","Almost immediately, the soldiers below rushed to turn the cannons. Some were crawling across the deck, dazed by the terrifying presence of the Titan... some were dead, having been turned into bloody stains. But no one had abandoned their duty. Nightwalker's Saints were all going all out to free their ship from the abomination’s grasp, as well.","But it was not going to be enough.","Perched on the creature's endless back and rending it to shreds with his ethereal fangs, Nightwalker could see the ground clearly. The devastated landscape of the abandoned battlefield beyond the walls of NQSC was drawing closer and closer.","They were not going to kill the Titan in time. They were not even going to sever its one remaining wing in time.","Even with Nightwalker expanding space to extend the calamitous fall, it was not enough — the world he was trying to reshape with his Will was permeated by the Will of the colossal Nightmare Creature, after all, slowing him down.","\"Goddammit!\"","Looking up, Nightwalker hesitated for a moment, then turned into a torrent of starlight and flashed toward the scarred and battered Mainmast Pagoda. Once inside, he slid across the floor of the runic hall and jumped to his feet, bending space to enter the runic circle in one step.","There, Naeve was standing on one knee, blood streaming down his face. The runic hall had sustained severe damage, but luckily enough, the circle itself was intact — steering the living ship without it was not impossible, but quite difficult.","\"Grab the rails!\"","Nightwalker's voice boomed across the entire main deck of the titanic vessel, sending the soldiers scurrying to grab something as if their lives depended on it. The Night Garden was supposed to keep them firmly standing on the deck no matter what maneuvers its helmsman had in mind, but with how damaged it was, there was no telling what would happen.","There was nothing to grab onto in the runic hall, though, so Naeve simply grabbed onto the belt of Nightwalker's armor.","The Night Garden careened, its bow moments away from crashing into the ground...","But just before it could, an enormous fissure opened in the fabric of reality, revealing an endless black void that was illuminated by countless stars and dreamlike nebulas.","The bow of the living ship plunged into the Dream Gate, which had opened parallel to the ground. The colossal fissure swallowed the entire great length of the Night Garden — from the runic hall, it looked as if they were falling into the starlit sky.","Then, the Mainmast Pagoda crossed the Dream Gate, as well.","A moment later, Nightwalker was blinded by brilliant light.","He was assaulted by unbearable heat.","The howling cacophony of the endless storm disappeared, replaced by a deafening litany of countless monstrous wails.","When Nightwalker's eyes adjusted to the light, what he saw...","Was a world on fire.","The Night Garden had exited the Dream Gate upside-down, momentum taking it higher into the azure sky. It was already spinning to right itself, but for now, all Nightwalker could see was the ground — the vast expanse of a sandy desert, all of it drowning in an ocean of silver flame. Myriads of Nightmare Creatures were moving in that flame, the black fractures of Nightmare Gates towering above them like dark pillars.","The air was full of winged abominations as well, all of them fusing into a harrowing swarm. Far in the distance, a battered city was unleashing a hail of explosive rounds into the swarm, streams of tracer rounds twisting like radiant snakes.","The terrifying sight was like a scene from hell... but it wasn't some distant inferno. The Night Garden gave Nightwalker the ability to open his Dream Gate between two points in the same realm, and that was what he had done, bringing his ship to the Western Quadrant.","They were currently in the Sahara Desert, where the forces of humanity were fighting a desperate battle against the advancing tide of abominations.","The hull of the Night Garden cracked precariously as the Titan tightened its coils, and since the titanic ship appeared right in the middle of a great swarm of winged abominations, those monsters were shifting their attention to its vast expanse as well. Nightwalker gritted his teeth.","“All battle crew below Transcendent Rank! Kill the vermin! Don't let a single bastard land!\"","As the Night Garden spun, aligning its main mast with the boundless sky above, the soldiers let go of the rails and unleashed a squall of attacks at the churning swarm. The Saints, meanwhile, kept attacking the Titan. Nightwalker swayed as the colossal creature's claws tore into the Mainmast Pagoda, then cursed and gazed at the swarming sky outside...","And there, he saw what he was looking for, moving like an annihilating shadow in the endless mass of abominations.","A great dragon with scales the color of the midnight sky was reigning terror in the sky above the ocean of flames, carving a path of destruction through the swarm. As Nightwalker watched, its enormous maw opened, and a haunting song resounded above the endless battlefield.","In the next moment, a blinding pillar of silver flame incinerated countless Nightmare Creatures, plunging toward the ground and cleaving a deadly path through the horde of abominations attacking the city.","Thousands of them were slaughtered in an instant, and more still perished as the dragon moved its head, sending the beam of silver death rolling across the desert. The sand boiled, turning into molten lava and flowing like a fiery sea.","Even if the dragon was too far for Nightwalker to see its eyes, he suddenly felt a heavy gaze crushing into him.","Smiling crookedly, he waved and then pointed to the enormous Titan strangling the ship.","The dragon studied him for a few moments and then changed course, moving swiftly in the direction of the Night Garden. Nightwalker let out a tired sigh, then laughed.","\"Damn it. Is his shift not over yet? I hoped to meet one of the young ladies instead...\"","Then, he helped Naeve to his feet, patted him on the shoulder, and turned into a stream of starlight again.","By the time Kai arrived, he was already rending the Titan's flesh. The Starbeast attacked the colossal abomination from the left, while the dragon descended upon it from the right like a dark mass of celestial fury.","Soon enough, rivers of blood flowed onto the deck of the Night Garden.","...An hour later, the Titan was dead. The swarm of winged abominations had been repelled, and the horde of Nightmare Creatures on the ground had turned to ash. The enemy was not defeated, but it was pushed back, for now — for a few days, or perhaps hours.","Or perhaps even minutes.","In the endless chaos of the end of days, nobody could say for sure.","Nightwalker was inspecting the damage when Kai landed on the bloody deck beside him, having already assumed his human form. The young man looked quite stunning, but also tired and grim — there were bruises under his eyes, and his skin was smeared with soot and dried blood.","Looking around, he grimaced.","“How bad is it?\"","Nightwalker cursed.","“Quite bad. The Night Garden is grievously wounded... I think I'll need to spend at least a few weeks at the wharf Lady Ananke built.\"","Needless to say, with the Night Garden disappearing for several weeks, the situation in the waking world was bound to turn from bad to worse.","Kai sighed.","\"Effie can cover for some of it... I'll talk to her.\"","Then, he closed his eyes for a moment, suppressing a groan.","When he opened them again, Nightwalker could already see that their conversation would be cut short.","Kai took a step back and nodded.","“I cannot stay any longer. Do not linger either — stay safe.\"","Saying that, Kai threw one last look at the devastated deck of the Night Garden and pulled himself across the realm boundary.","A few heartbeats later, the unbearable strike of the vast desert, a great swath of it turned to glass, was replaced by unbearable cold. The winds howled, throwing sharp ice crystals into his face. The air smelled of blood and ash, and he was plunged into the clamor of battle once more.","Kai sighed and looked ahead.","In front of him were the spires of the Jade Palace, and beyond them, on the plain below the mountains, a great blizzard was devouring the world. He could see the shapes of countless snow wraiths moving under the cover of the blizzard, and the banners of Seishan's legion fluttering in the wind like a river of blood.","With his miraculous sight, he saw it all — Seishan and her sisters, their Transcendent champions, Ascended officers, Awakened soldiers, Beastmaster's thralls shielding the humans with their bodies, countless Echoes throwing themselves into the mass of enemies, the Ravenous Fiend moving through the blizzard like an obliterating mountain of fire and steel...","Mundane soldiers were manning the fortifications that protected the city, and more Awakened were bracing themselves as the towering, churning white wall of the blizzard drew closer to the vast expanse of scarlet fields.","He also saw three colossal shapes moving far in the distance, guiding the blizzard like profane shepherds. Each of them was tall enough to dwarf mountains and eerie enough to make even his blood run cold. Kai inhaled deeply and summoned his bow.","“It just never ends, does it?\"","He nocked an arrow and launched himself into the swirling snow.","Then again, perhaps it was good that the battle never ended.","Life was war, after all.","The day all fighting ceased would be the day all humans were gone.","For now, though, they were still here.","They were still fighting."]},{"number":3209,"title":"Chapter 3209 Merry Men","paragraphs":["A carriage was rolling down a forest road, pulled by a black steed. Its curtains were closed, and there was no sound coming from the interior. There was a young man sitting on the coachman’s bench, holding the reins with a steady hand. His skin was like porcelain, and his eyes were like glistening onyx; with nothing but rustling trees in sight, he seemed to be enjoying a moment of peace.","That peace did not last long, though. Suddenly, one of the trees fell across the road, barring the path of a carriage, and a ragtag crowd of armed men burst from the underbrush to surround it.","\"Well, well, well... what do we have here?\"","Their leader was a towering man with a bushy beard, wearing makeshift leather armor. Resting a monstrous cleaver on his shoulder, he gave the gilded ornaments of the carriage a look of avarice and then shifted his menacing gaze to the coachman.","\"Hey there, little friend. Where are you heading?\"","A sinister grin split his face apart.","The coachman scratched the tip of his nose awkwardly and remained silent for a few moments. Eventually, he sighed and said:","“To be honest, I am heading to the Shadow Realm.\"","The bandits exploded with laughter. Their leader, too, was amused by the answer.","“Prepared to die? Ha! It seems you've recognized me, the Forest King — the butcher of men, Ascended Cleaver! Ah, but do not worry. I am not at all as bloodthirsty as stories tell.\"","He chuckled menacingly.","\"Tell you what. Give us the horse, the carriage, all the money you have, and your clothes. Then, after we dragged your master from the carriage and stripped them of all earthly possessions... if you kill your master with your own two hands, we will spare your life and allow you to join us!\"","The coachman looked at him with a hint of confusion in his black eyes.","After a short while, he decided to clarify.","“Just to be sure. You want me and the person in the carriage to fight to the death... naked?\"","The leader of the bandits — the self-proclaimed Forest King, Cleaver, blinked a couple of times. He glanced back at his subordinates, who were giving him weird glances, then coughed.","“On second thought, you can strip naked after you've killed them.\"","The coachman frowned slightly.","“Won't I be one of you guys by then? Why would I strip naked?\"","The towering bandit sighed.","\"Are you giving us money or not? I've already decided to cut off your tongue, smartass, but you can still make it out of here alive.\"","The coachman waved a hand.","\"No, no... you can have my money.\"","With that, he pulled out a small pouch, untied it, and shook it a few times. A dozen or so coins poured into his palm, some of them glistening gold. The eyes of the bandits shone when they saw it.","Before the coachman could hand them the money, though, there was the sound of something falling inside the carriage, followed by the clinking of bottles and a low, tortured groan.","Then, one of the curtains was pulled back, and a devilishly handsome young man with a crescent moon mark on his forehead emerged, hanging out of the window.","He seemed to be in his early twenties. His eyes were bloodshot, and he looked extremely miserable, as if suffering from a dreadful hangover.","The bandits who stood close to the carriage paled and took a step back, pinching their noses. The stench of alcohol was almost unbearable.","The young man looked at the scene in front of him with blurry eyes. Then, he seemed to regain a sliver of awareness.","Looking at the Forest King and the coachman, who froze with a pile of coins in his hand, the young man rubbed his eyes. Then, he studied them for a few more moments and let out a startled chuckle.","\"Who are these clowns, Shadow?\"","His eyes widened.","“Wait... are we getting robbed? We are actually getting robbed?!\"","The coachman nodded.","\"That's pretty evident.\"","The young man stared at him in utter disbelief.","\"And you are actually giving them the money?!\"","The coachman shrugged.","“I don't really need money. They seem to have more use for it.”","His supposed master scoffed.","Then, his gaze suddenly turned sharp.","\"Wait... is this one of your sick games? It is, isn't it?!\"","He shuddered, then looked at the bandits with a strange expression.","Cleaver could have sworn that it was... pity.","“It's not. Really.\"","The young master opened the door of the carriage and stumbled out of it, making the bandits grimace and take another step back.","“As if I'd believe that!\"","At that point, Cleaver's patience ran out.","\"Hey, bastards! I don't think you two are taking this situation seriously enough! I am going to cut off your limbs, make you eat them, and then skin you alive! I'll mince your bodies into tiny pieces and feed you to the dogs!\"","He huffed angrily, but then hesitated for a moment.","Finally, he asked in a lower tone:","“But just in case... what do you mean by sick games? What sick things can this little brat be guilty of?\"","The young master rolled his eyes.","\"Don't get me started!\"","Looking at the coachman with resentful eyes, he spat.","\"If I were you, I'd apologize and run away. No, better walk away slowly! Don't make sudden moves... don't provoke him! He made an oath not to kill anyone!\"","The bandit leader tilted his head in confusion.","“Wait, isn't that good news for me? Here I was, feeling a little apprehensive. But if he can't even kill anyone, then there's nothing to fear?\"","The young master shook his head energetically, then paled and grabbed it, letting out another groan.","“No, no... that just shows how uncultured you are, with no foresight! You'd think that if a person can't kill you, you are safe. But it's the opposite! Just because he can't kill you doesn't mean that he can't make you wish you were dead!\"","He leaned tiredly on the carriage.","“Like that time we passed through a sinful city stricken by a mystical plague. That guy found the Spirit Rat responsible for the plague, and, well... I had never seen a rat shedding tears before, let alone a Sacred Rat. But that one! That one was crying and rubbing its little paws together, as if begging to be killed. Actually, there were a myriad of them, and they all begged at the same time.\"","The bandit leader blinked.","The young master wasn't done, though.","“Or that other time, during the Divine Vigil... all the heroes of the mortal realms gathered to send War God's avatar on her way, and a few Supremes came as well. That sick bastard developed a dislike for the Second Wandering Archon, so he challenged the poor man to a debate and argued with him for seven days straight. On the seventh day, the Archon spat blood and collapsed, his hair turning white, tears flowing out of his eyes like ceaseless rivers. His Domain completely collapsed! I hear he hasn't uttered a word since.\"","The bandit scratched the back of his head.","“The Second Wandering Archon? No way. That elder withstood two blows from the Demon of Dread once...\"","The young master scoffed.","“The Demon of Dread?! Let me tell you about dread, fool! Once, we met an arrogant Spirit who ravaged a realm over a perceived slight. That guy over there couldn't kill it, so instead, he broke its body, shattered its soul, and extinguished its spirit — not enough for that unfortunate deity to die, but just shy of it. Spirits are pretty hardy, though. So, he waited for that one to heal... then repeated the whole thing, ten times in a row. And he had no plans of stopping, either! Eventually, the High Priest of Heart God's cult had to arrive and personally plead for their Spirit.\"","The bandit leader waited for a few moments, then asked cautiously:","“Well? And what happened then?\"","The young master groaned and covered his face with a palm.","\"The Heart God's cult has a new High Priest now. The old one retired and became a hermit... after he regained the ability to walk without crutches, that is. He still screams in his sleep, though!\"","The coachman gave him a gloomy look.","\"I did spare the Spirit though, didn't I?\"","The bandit leader studied the two of them silently for a while, then growled and pointed his enormous cleaver at the young master.","“Who do you take me for, noble scum?! A complete idiot?! Sacred Beasts, Supreme monarchs, Spirits, and High Priests?! What kind of human is capable of facing them in a fight, let alone surviving it?! And what, that bastard is serving as a coachman?! Who are you then, a god's avatar?! Let me guess, that horse is a Sacred Beast as well!\"","The young master spared him a pitying glance, then sighed and shook his head.","\"You made three mistakes, blockhead.\"","He pointed at the horse.","\"First, this is not a horse. This is a mass of shadows shaped to look like a horse. Why? I have no idea. That guy just seems to like black horses, for some reason.\"","Then, he pointed to himself.","\"Second, I am not a god's avatar. I am merely a god's grandson. Her favorite grandson, of course! But still, not an avatar.\"","Finally, he pointed to the coachman.","\"And finally... that thing is not a human. It's a Supreme Titan created by the God of Death to punish all living things. It's just pretending to be human because... well, I don't know. He's just perverted that way, I guess.\"","The bandit leader scoffed and stared at them with murder in his eyes, clearly unconvinced.","But then, his eyes shifted slightly toward the black horse.","At some point in time, the horse's silhouette had grown strangely vague, and wisps of ethereal black smoke were drifting from its mouth.","The horse slowly lost its shape, like a melting candle. And beneath that deceptive shape, he saw...","A terrified scream resounded in the forest, sending a flock of birds flying in fright.","\"R-run! Run!\"","Dropping his cleaver, the bandit leader turned around and dashed away, his eyes full of primal horror. His subordinates were of lesser Ranks, so they weren't quite as fast — still, in just a few moments, all of them disappeared into the forest.","Several black tentacles shot from the shapeless mass of shadows.","Instead of pursuing the bandits, though, they simply grabbed the tree barring the road and flung it aside.","A heartbeat later, there was a normal black horse in front of the carriage once again, nibbling docilely on the fallen leaves. Shadow sighed and dropped the coins back into the purse.","“I only got into a spat with that Spirit because you kept threatening to fight it yourself, you know. So... that was unfair.\"","Noctis waved a hand and climbed back into the carriage.","\"Whatever. I am hungover... wake me up when we're there.\"","Closing the door, he lowered the curtains. Shadow nudged the horse, and the carriage continued to roll forward.","A few minutes later, Snuggle climbed out of his pocket and jumped down to the bench, sitting beside him.","She pretended to yawn.","\"See? That's progress! You didn't even want to kill them, did you?\"","Shadow spared her a glance.","“Wrong. I did want to kill them.\"","He leaned back and looked into the depths of the forest with a wistful expression.","“This time, they stumbled onto us. Who will be their victim the next time? Someone weaker than I am, no doubt. How many people will lose their lives because I spared these few?\"","He shrugged with a detached smile.","“Not that I care. It's just for the sake of the argument... mercy is not always a virtue, Snuggle.”","The little doll stared at him for a while, then shook her head.","“This is not to save other lives, though. It's to save yours.\"","Shadow laughed.","\"I am neither truly alive nor something that can die. So saving me from death is a misguided endeavor.\"","Snuggle studied him some more, then looked away dejectedly.","Soon enough, they reached their destination.","Up ahead, the forest receded, making space for a vast expanse of emerald grass. In the distance, golden fields stretched as far as the eye could see.","The air was permeated by a sense of bliss and tranquility.","The dirt road turned into one cobbled with stone, and the carriage rolled through a beautiful stone arch.","At the top of the arch, a few runes were carved into the white stone...","They read:","Kingdom of Hope."]},{"number":3210,"title":"Chapter 3210 Fear of Hope","paragraphs":["The carriage crossed the arch and continued on its way. Shadow's expression did not change, but he turned his head slightly, looking north.","Their long journey across the mortal realms was nearing its end.","It had taken them a few years to reach the Kingdom of Hope — the last mortal realm they had to cross before reaching the Hollow Mountains.","Noctis was not nineteen anymore. His face had lost the last traces of adolescence, and he did not look like a boy now, resembling a man more and more with each day. Snuggle and Shadow, meanwhile, remained the same... at least outwardly.","In truth, many things had happened during their journey, so neither of them was the same.","Even if Shadow did not want to, he had allowed himself to be pulled deeper into the whirlpool of humanity. After meeting countless people and witnessing their lives, often becoming an unwilling participant in their joys and conflicts, he had no choice but to become painted in similar hues. He was now much more human than he had been or ever wished to be.","Snuggle seemed to have changed the least. She had grown more comfortable with her Transcendent powers, learning more about her Aspect and its depths — but apart from that, the little doll was just as cheerful and clumsy as before.","It was just that now there was a dark undertone hidden behind her brightness, even more so than there had been in the past.","That was because now that they had spent so much time together, both Shadow and Snuggle had an inkling of who the other one was. It was just that nothing good could come from knowing the truth, so both of them avoided broaching the subject, even in their thoughts.","There were enough things happening every day to keep them occupied, anyway.","In hindsight, meeting Noctis had been a blessing. If Shadow and Snuggle — an ancient Titan and a homeless soul occupying a child's doll — ventured into the cauldron of the mortal realms alone, they would have probably left a trail of ruin and devastation in their wake, eventually attracting the attention of beings who were too powerful even for Shadow to face.","He was not the most sociable of creatures, after all. Even if he did not want to get entangled with the world, the world rarely left him a chance to stay detached from it, and since Shadow wasn't really familiar with such concepts as humility, fear, and knowing when to shut up, things were bound to get complicated when the world came knocking.","His propensity to always tell the truth alone was disastrous.","But with Noctis there to shield Shadow from the countless people and beings they had met on the way, most of their journey had been somewhat smooth. Noctis was not only able to smooth things over, but had also proven himself useful in countless ways, from renting rooms at inns to navigating the complicated web of relationships between the great powers of the mortal realms.","It was just that the young Transcendent's usefulness had its own drawback, as well. There were many things that Shadow would have passed by indifferently, but Noctis refused to.","So... their journey had not been entirely smooth, after all.","In fact, it was full of twists and turns, conflicts and unexpected resolutions. Noctis and Snuggle handled the Creatures of Corruption — those they could handle, at least. Shadow stepped in when things became too perilous.","Like those two Sacred beings Noctis had mentioned. The way he told the tale to the bandits, both of them had been easy prey to Shadow... of course, it wasn't true. In fact, it was the exact opposite of the truth.","After testing himself against these two Sacred beings, Shadow came to the conclusion that while he could handle some, each of such battles would be a matter of life and death. Sacred beings were different from each other, after all. Just like there were people who were weak and people who were paragons of martial skill, Spirits were not created equal either.","Among those who were Supreme, Shadow was like a herald of death. Even if he had promised not to kill, he could still devastate most opponents of his own Rank with relative ease. In a battle against those who were Sacred, however... even if he could hold his own, the outcome was up to luck.","Shadow had a feeling that if he stumbled on a truly powerful Spirit one day, he would be destroyed. Of course, he wasn't really afraid of death.","But every time he had died in the past, he was thrust into a new life.","So if there was something Shadow feared, it was life.","With a sigh, he guided their carriage across a well-maintained stone road. Around them, the tranquil vista of the Kingdom of Hope sprawled toward the horizon. The vast expanse of emerald grass, the golden fields in the distance, the boundless blue sky above — the scene was blissful and picturesque, infused with a feeling of peace.","Among all the places they had visited, this land — a mortal realm ruled by a Divine being — seemed like the safest. From what Shadow had heard, people here thrived. Their lives were not without worries, of course, but far better than in most places.","And yet, Shadow could not help but feel a chill run down his spine.","The moment they entered the Kingdom of Hope, he suddenly felt disturbed and uneasy. Looking at the beautiful landscape around them, all he could hear was the rattling of chains.","All he could think about were memories of madness.","Unable to stop himself, Shadow turned his head and glanced at the carriage, where Noctis was still sleeping off his recent escapade.","Shadow's expression darkened.","Just at that moment, the door of the carriage opened, and Noctis climbed onto the coachman’s bench while yawning.","\"I told you to wake me up, did I not?\"","“H—hey, watch it!\"","In his groggy state, he didn't notice Snuggle and almost sat on her, forcing the little doll to scurry closer to Shadow and give him a resentful look.","“You stink!\"","Noctis scoffed.","“So what? You don't have a nose.\"","Shadow smiled quietly.","Noctis, meanwhile, glanced around with curiosity.","\"So this is the Kingdom of Hope.\"","His eyes glinted with wonder.","\"The Demon of Desire has always been fond of humans, but it's still a bit strange, isn't it? For her to establish a kingdom in the mortal realms. I heard she is a wise and benevolent ruler.\"","He smiled.","“And she invented writing, too!\"","His admiring smile widened a little, then suddenly disappeared. Noctis remained silent for a short while, then said with a dark expression on his face:","\"Come to think of it, I had to endure all those exhausting reading lessons because of her. Shadow, do you know the horror of having to stay inside and read when the weather outside is perfectly fine? Actually, don't answer. You spent thousands of years in a damp cave. You'd probably love it, lunatic!\"","Shadow shrugged.","Noctis sighed heavily, then shivered.","\"Still, it's weird. The rest of the daemons are so aloof and terrifying, but the Demon of Desire seems... nice.\"","Shadow looked at him, then turned his gaze back to the road.","\"Really? I think differently.\"","His faint smile dimmed a little.","\"I think she is the most terrifying of them all.\"","Noctis and Snuggle both glanced at him with surprise.","\"Really? Why?\"","He did not answer for a while, then leaned back and sighed.","“All things start from desire. And all things bow to desire, as well.\"","Noctis scoffed.","“Sounds like a lot of rubbish...\"","Looking ahead, they could just see the walls of a bustling city. Noctis seemed to liven up, expecting to rest from the road soon.","The closer to the city they got, the more people there were on the road. Carts, carriages, and wagons moved both ways, and from time to time, a horseman would fly by, rushing on some unknown business. There were some traveling on foot, as well — their faces were relaxed and healthy, as if they knew no fear of the Creatures of Corruption.","That, at least, made sense. What kind of Nightmare Creature would be bold enough to enter a land ruled by a Divine Titan?","Noctis seemed more and more pleased. It seemed that he was already imagining the wonders of local cuisine and culture — or maybe he was simply looking forward to curing his hangover with some wine. However, Shadow led their carriage around the city without approaching its gate. Noctis was startled.","“Huh? Wait, where are we going?\"","Shadow kept looking ahead.","“There's a place I want to visit.\"","Despite the protests of the young man, the carriage rolled forward, soon leaving the city behind.","Before too long, towering white walls revealed themselves in front of them once again.","Not too far from the city, a magnificent structure stood under the boundless sky, emanating an overpowering feeling of joy and excitement.","It was a great colosseum built of white stone."]},{"number":3211,"title":"Chapter 3211 The Queen’s Riddle","paragraphs":["The coliseum had been built by the Demon of Desire herself, and was called the Theater of Hope. Its walls were white and pristine, as if built from the pure clouds that traveled across the azure sky — however, as Shadow glanced up at the magnificent arches, he couldn't help but imagine them adorned with banners that were as red as blood.","An echo of a distant chant surfaced from his memory:","“Glory! Glory! Glory!\"","Shadow winced, feeling a ghostly pain pierce his chest. A moment later, the ghastly vision was gone, and the pain was gone as well.","There was indeed an exuberant chant resounding from within the great theater, but it had nothing to do with glory. Instead, the jubilant voices of a vast crowd were calling for the performers to enter the stage.","It seemed that a play was about to begin — Shadow and his companions had arrived just in time.","“I've heard so many stories about the Theater of Hope! They say that there is nothing like it in the world.”","Noctis grinned, clearly excited.","Snuggle seemed quite curious, as well. Shadow lingered for a moment, then said in a calm tone:","“Then what are we waiting for?\"","Leaving the carriage below the walls of the great theater, they paid a small fee and entered. Inside, a vast arena was surrounded by soaring rows of stone benches, all of them filled by expectant spectators. Sunshine poured from above, reflecting from white stone and creating a beautiful, dreamlike atmosphere.","The sounds of laughter and excited chatter washed over Shadow and his companions, making them feel a bit of warm anticipation as well.","Even Shadow, who was rarely enthusiastic about anything, felt like he was looking forward to the play.","He frowned, then shivered slightly.","‘Such potent sorcery...’","Indeed, that feeling of anticipation was not entirely his own. Looking around, he noticed shallow channels carved into the stone throughout the great theater. The entire enormous coliseum was one vast runic array — Shadow could not quite discern its purpose yet, but it seemed to enhance the emotions of people gathered inside.","The sorcery of the Theater of Hope was truly astonishing... and terrifying. It wasn't easy to affect the heart of a Supreme Titan, and yet that was exactly what had happened — without him noticing, no less.","Noctis had said that the Demon of Desire was nice, but Shadow felt nothing but cold dread when thinking about her.","His companions, however, succumbed to the atmosphere of her theater easily, igniting with excitement.","“Shadow! Let's go find a good seat!\"","Hearing Snuggle's squeaky voice, Shadow pulled himself out of his short reverie and went to do just that. Soon enough, the three of them were seated in one of the higher rows of the Theater of Hope — Shadow and Noctis resting on the benches, Snuggle sitting on one of Shadow's shoulders.","The vast arena was below them. It was circular, and at its center stood the stage.","“Look, look! It's starting!\"","Snuggle pulled at Shadow's hair to make him pay attention, which only made him wince.","There was movement in the arena, indeed.","As if out of nowhere, a tall figure appeared on the stage, wearing a white robe and a smiling mask. The audience exploded with excited shouts, while the figure — the leader of the chorus, coryphaeus — bowed and performed a few movements of a simple, elegant dance.","When the audience grew quiet, a booming voice resounded from beneath the smiling mask. The Theater of Hope was vast, and yet Shadow could hear each word clearly, as if the coryphaeus was standing directly in front of him. It was partially due to the unique acoustics of the theater, and partially due to the actor's masterful delivery.","The play began.","At first, Shadow was only mildly interested in the story. But as it progressed, told by the masked actors and the chorus, he felt himself being drawn into it. The singing of the chorus and the voices of the actors fused with the unique sorcery of the Theater of Hope, creating an unforgettable mixture.","The story of the play was one he knew, but not in detail.","It was the story of the beautiful and enigmatic ruler of a mystical land of ash and snow... the Jade Queen.","At the start of the play, the Jade Queen was a young and innocent monster. She was born in the crystalline darkness and spent her days enthusiastically searching for miraculous nectar. Then, however, her beauty and innocence caught the eye of the Demon of Dread, who was passing by during his journey to the mortal realms. Bored, the Demon of Dread decided to become the young monster's teacher. The first act of the play was light and comedic in tone, describing the many clashes between the terrifying daemon's desire to make the Jade Queen into a proper young lady and her mischievous, inhuman nature. Eventually, the Jade Queen learned how to speak the human language and Transcended, gaining a Transformation Ability — it was just that since she was a creature, and not a human, her Transformation Ability worked the other way around and allowed her to become one.","At the end of the first act, the Demon of Dread whispered something into her ear — he taught her a terrible truth that no one else knew, causing the end of the Jade Queen's childhood.","Shadow had an inkling of what that truth was, but the playwright didn't. So, the play never stated it either.","‘I wonder how much of what is shown in the play is true.'","In the second act, the Jade Queen had already become a young woman. She was now a ruler of a distant, mystical realm — wise and enlightened, but also willful, capricious, and at times downright sinister. Nevertheless, the news of her enchanting beauty and profound wisdom spread far and wide, stirring the hearts of many heroes.","Many suitors arrived to pursue her. Some failed to cross the great bridge leading to her Jade Palace, some made it through and were welcomed in her court, but ultimately refused. Some harbored impure thoughts and were punished for their vices in ghastly, horrible ways. Eventually, the Jade Queen grew tired of these advances and issued a challenge to all the mortal realms. If someone could solve her riddle, she would fulfill any wish that person had. After the second act ended, Shadow found himself unable to decide whether the Jade Queen was a benevolent being or a creature full of malice. She was endearing and tantalizing, no doubt... her wisdom and insight were unrivaled. But what was hidden behind the jade mask?","What did the Jade Queen desire? What did she fear? Everyone knew of her, but no one seemed to care who she was.","Maybe that was the purpose of the deadly riddle — not to find a worthy consort among the sea of suitors, but to find someone who could share the heavy burden of forbidden knowledge she carried in her heart.","The third act showed the gathering of guests who arrived in hopes of solving the riddle and receiving a wish from the beautiful, frightening Jade Queen. The tone of the third act was not at all comedic, but Noctis spent its entirety laughing... that was because there were many familiar faces among the Jade Queen's guests.","\"By the moon... aren't they the pompous brothers, sons of Sun God? They visited the temple once. I stole the older one's sword!\"","“Ah, the Mason! That Transcendent uncle is such a bore. Actually, the priests who raised me were all over him, forgetting all shame. That is because nobody can build a temple more magnificent than those built by him — he built one for Sun God, War God, Storm God, Heart God... so, they couldn't endure the thought that grandma doesn't have one as well! I swear, if he put just a fraction of the time he spends on building things into fighting Creatures of Corruption, he'd be Supreme a long time ago.”","\"Wait, is that supposed to be... me?! What the hell, I never went to find the Jade Queen! I was a toddler when this gathering happened, damn it!\"","Shadow spared him a casual glance and smiled.","Indeed, many heroes gathered to solve the Jade Queen's riddle. In fact, not all of them wanted to become her consort — some were simply attracted by the promise of a wish being fulfilled. There were not that many Supremes in the world, after all, not to mention Supremes favored by one of the great and terrible daemons. So, a promise made by the Jade Queen was worth a lot. None of the illustrious heroes managed to solve the riddle, though. The warriors failed, and the sages failed as well.","In the end, a figure wearing tattered rags emerged from the crowd of guests, the eyes of her mask covered by a dirty blindfold. She was a mad oracle from a distant land — a land where people did not worship gods, and built temples to fate instead.","The great heroes treated her with contempt, but the Jade Queen seemed amused. So, she asked the oracle the same question:","“What is the heaviest thing in the world?\"","The mad oracle laughed bitterly and then answered, pointing at her unseeing eyes.","\"It's knowledge.\"","And thus, the riddle was solved.","The play ended with the chorus singing about enlightenment and knowledge, praising the wise queen and the learned oracle.","The audience seemed to be greatly satisfied, exploding with applause and whistles.","Shadow, however, thought that the ending of the play was quite strange.","Neither the Jade Queen nor the blind oracle seemed that fond of the truths they bore, so why would the playwright paint pursuit of knowledge as a noble virtue? Trying to attach a didactic moral to the story only seemed forced and patronizing.","More than that, where was the real ending? What was the wish of the blind oracle, and did the Jade Queen make it come true? Surely, that mad oracle wasn't aiming to become the beautiful queen's consort...","‘What a strange play.’","Shadow sighed and shook his head.","Even if he did not like the ending, the experience of watching a play in the Theater of Hope was truly wondrous. The songs of the chorus, the dancing, the twists and turns of the story... he was swept up by the blazing emotions of the crowd, feeling more joyful and exhilarated than ever before.","In this life, at least.","And while none of the spectators could perceive it, Shadow had learned quite a lot about the sorcery of Hope, as well."]},{"number":3212,"title":"Chapter 3212 A Girl Whom Nobody Loved","paragraphs":["In Shadow's memories, the Theater of Hope was a ghastly place.","Many of his lives had ended here — some succumbing to terrible wounds in the cages below the arena, some on its blood-red surface. His blood and the jubilation of the frenzied crowd fueled the sorcery of the great coliseum, so he had assumed that it was a sinister and malevolent kind of magic. However, now that he had witnessed the Theater of Hope in its original state, he realized that he was wrong.","It wasn't the deaths of caged slaves that fueled the sorcery that the Demon of Desire had created, and neither was it their blood. Instead, it was the spectators.","Their emotions, to be precise.","As Shadow observed the play, he saw torrents of soul essence flowing through the vast runes carved into the white stone of Hope's coliseum. The source of that soul essence was the jubilant crowd — the more excited and exhilarated the audience members were, the more essence there was. Enthralled by the singing of the chorus and the powerful voices of the actors, they fueled the theater.","However, they did not fuel it with their own soul essence. Shadow did not know how, but it was their emotions themselves that were transformed into mystical energy... truly, a sorcery worthy of one of the daemons.","The source of the soul essence was interesting. Far more interesting, however, was the target of the vast enchantment. Shadow was not powerful or knowledgeable enough to discern the secrets of divine sorcery, but he did manage to glean its core purpose.","The smaller measure of the powerful enchantment was channeled back into the great theater, enhancing the enjoyment of the crowd, making it more susceptible to the mundane power of the engaging performance.","A far greater measure, however, was channeled directly into the depths of the Kingdom of Hope, nourishing it. Shadow was not sure what exact form that nourishment took, but he was certain that the Theater of Hope was nurturing and protecting this land.","It was rather ingenious.","In the hands of the Demon of Desire, the great theater was a joyous and benevolent force that benefitted the people of her kingdom.","In the hands of those who would come after her... it would become the monstrous Red Colosseum, a blood-soaked altar of War. Which was not to say that the Red Colosseum did not benefit people. It was just that its power would serve a far more malevolent purpose in the hands of its future owner.","\"That was great, wasn't it?\"","Noctis seemed satisfied, at least.","\"Now that's culture... ah, the costumes, the poetry! Simply marvelous.\"","The young Transcendent grinned.","\"Even if the mask they used to portray me is not nearly handsome enough! But, oh well. Is there even an artisan in the world who can capture my dashing visage?\"","Snuggle gave him a sideways glance.","“The better question is if there is an actor in the world who can portray your vanity...\"","Shadow smiled faintly, but he was only listening to them half-heartedly. As they left the great theater, he could not help but look at its pristine white walls.","Once again, his memories were stirring, and he felt powerless to resist them.","He remembered one of his past lives — a fierce and defiant life painted in shades of red.","In that life... he was a girl whom nobody loved.","She was born in the slums of a prosperous city. Her father did not care enough to name her, vanishing into the dark alleys. Her mother saw her as a burden and abandoned her on the dirty streets. The people who saw her were only full of irritation and anger. From those times, all she remembered was hunger and loneliness... and scorn.","Luckily, she was born with hair of a color that was unusual in these parts. Orphaned girls with red hair were often entrusted to an ancient order of female warriors, and while her hair was chestnut, someone decided that it was close enough. So, she was brought to a temple instead of starving or freezing to death on the streets. She was too young to understand what a warrior was or who the gods were — all she knew was that she was warm in the temple, and the adults gave her food for free.","In the temple, she was not alone anymore. She was even given a name.","Life in the temple was not easy. The girls adopted by the priestesses underwent grueling training and thorough education. Those who showed promise were given more attention; those who fell short were raised to be temple slaves or cast out.","Some died.","She did not want to die, but she did not mind becoming a slave. If anything, the girls who had been deemed unworthy of becoming warriors led a much easier life... and yet, she trained harder than anyone else.","That was because, even if she did not understand it clearly, she wanted attention. There were many orphans like her, after all, but only a few priestesses who trained them. Their time was a treasure that was difficult to win.","Attention was not love, but back then, she did not understand the difference. Even if the former tasted hollow, she wanted it all the same. And so, she strived to be the best. She wasn't the strongest among the girls in the temple, and she wasn't the fastest. She wasn't even the smartest... but there was one thing that separated her from the rest. It was that she never gave up.","No matter how painful or difficult, she always pushed forward. Every time she fell, she got up. She endured the bruises, the callouses, the bloodstains. She walked forward, one step at a time.","After a while, she grew stronger, faster, and smarter. As the number of girls on the training field dwindled, her dedication never waned. Soon enough, none of them could defeat her... and that was why they treated her coldly, just like everyone else had.","But she had talent, it seemed.","In fact, her talent was monstrous.","At ten, she slew her first Beast.","At twelve, she learned how to sense soul essence.","At fourteen, she Awakened.","At sixteen, full of vitality and delicate beauty of youth, she unsealed her Aspect. None of the Awakened priestesses in the temple could defeat her anymore.","That was when everything changed. The priestesses who had been cold and distant before slowly started to treat her with warmth and affection. Her fellow disciples, who had always been hostile and unfriendly, were suddenly nice and attentive.","She was happy...","For a while.","But then, things began to turn for the worse.","The priestesses never left her alone, often quarreling among each other about who would spend time with her. Their attention, which she had always desired, became burdensome instead of sweet.","The other young disciples were worse. Their eyes, their smiles, their voices... all of it began to unnerve her. They were too intense, too possessive.","Almost obsessed.","It wasn't long before blood was spilled.","That was how she discovered her Flaw — her cruel, bitter Flaw.","It was that people could not help but love her.","The more time they spent with her, the greater their love became, the more they desired to never be apart from her.","To always be with her... to possess her. That longing eventually drove them mad. Some lasted longer, while some surrendered almost immediately. But in the end, they all succumbed.","Needless to say, that caused quite a problem for the temple.","...At seventeen, she was sent to war.","Now a true War Maiden, having given the oath, she entered the battlefield as a priestess of War God. Things were easier on the battlefield, because no one lived long enough to become infatuated with her. There was blood, there were torn bodies, there were screams of agony and death. There were young soldiers calling for their mothers.","She did not call, because she did not remember hers.","Her world became painted red.","She was cut, battered, and broken. She was pierced by sharp blades and mauled by sharp claws. She fell into dirt and rose from piles of bodies. She learned horror, sorrow, and triumph.","And she never gave up.","Her enemies died. Her comrades died, as well. Those who survived... she kept a distance from them, knowing that they would slowly become enthralled otherwise.","She was lonely.","One war ended, and another started. She traveled from one battlefield to another, undefeated, growing stronger. Growing fearsome. Slowly, her fame spread, and people began to seek her out — not because of her beauty, but because of her strength. Because they wanted her to fight for them. But even bathed in their attention, in their desire, she still felt alienated. There was an invisible wall between her and everyone else.","In her journeys, there was only one being who kept her company.","There was only one being whom she never had to abandon, and who never died.","Who was always by her side.","It was her goddess... the Goddess of War.","Finally, turning twenty, she realized a simple truth.","It was that War God was her mother, her sister, and her companion.","For as long as War God existed, she would never be alone.","She would always be loved."]},{"number":3213,"title":"Chapter 3213 Thousands of Years of Corruption","paragraphs":["Life was war, and war was everywhere in the tumultuous ocean of the mortal realms. Now that generations of valiant heroes had pushed the previous rulers of the mundane world back and civilization had blossomed, Creatures of Corruption hid in the dark corners of existence and remote lands. Even if they had not disappeared altogether, many people went their entire lives without meeting one.","And without the Creatures of Corruption, those same heroes who had fought them turned their gazes to each other.","Cities grew and turned into kingdoms; the borders of the kingdoms pressed against each other, and conflicts abounded. More than that, exalted champions rose to the throne of Supremacy from time to time — and every time a new Supreme was crowned, they had to establish a Domain. Old borders collapsed, and new ones were established. The balance of power in the mortal realms was disturbed, and a devastating wave of change rolled outward across the world, reaching even those realms that were far apart from the rising Domains.","So, war was common.","And a priestess of War always had somewhere to go.","Released from the torment of solitude, she was unbound. She had been too young and too naive when she gave the oath and became a War Maiden — but after maturing and treading the red mud of blood-soaked battlefields, she finally understood its tenets. She finally fathomed the true essence of War and learned true devotion. Her goddess was the goddess of war... but ultimately, she was the goddess of life.","War was life, and life always triumphed. It always persevered, it always endured. It never gave up.","Just like her.","So, what she truly worshipped was life.","And there was nowhere one could experience life sharper or more desperately than on a battlefield — surrounded by death, only the width of a blade away from falling into its dark embrace.","Now that she was twenty and already an Ascended, having devoted herself to her goddess, she finally felt like herself. She felt as if it was only now that she gained the ability to think for herself and make her own decisions... to be her own person.","She wasn't a novice among the War Maidens anymore, either, and as such was afforded authority. One of the privileges she gained was the right to lead younger sisters into battle; the other was to decide which battlefield to enter on her own.","Each War Maiden had her own way of choosing where to worship their goddess, and for which side to fight. Some fought for those who seemed to have a nobler cause; some fought for those who had more valor. Some pursued opportunities to witness specific stratagems or test themselves against outstanding warriors.","For her, the choice was simple. She always went where the drums of war roared the loudest, joining the fiercest of battles to fight for the weakest side. Her goal was always to cut down the strongest adversaries while ensuring that as many of her comrades as possible survived. She was often grievously wounded, but never defeated — wherever she went, blood flowed like a river, but she never drowned in its tide.","She witnessed the ugliest side of humanity. She witnessed the most beautiful expressions of human goodness, as well. She witnessed life in all its brilliant glory — from the darkest hues of despair and sorrow to the radiant joy of devotion and hope.","She fought men. She fought Creatures of Corruption.","She watched, she learned... she grew.","At twenty-six, she became a Transcendent. Soon, there was an army following her. Her name was renowned across all mortal realms, and her fame continued to rise.","But the desire of those who wanted to claim her continued to grow, as well, as did their power. They came to break her and force her to submit, to make her their own...","She faced and killed them all.","Eventually, she grew tired of bloodshed. And so, for a while, she retreated from the world, returning to the temple that had nurtured her — there, she took charge of raising a new generation of War Maidens, treating the orphaned girls as her own daughters.","Some of them were motivated. Some of them were lazy. Some of them were strong and talented, while some were weak and unsuited for combat. But still, she loved them all. Even if she had to keep her distance to spare them the curse of her Flaw, she made sure to give each one as much attention as she could.","She was gentler than the priestesses who had raised her... perhaps that was her sin. The goal of all War Maidens was to reforge themselves in the image of the goddess they worshiped. That goddess was a goddess of war, but she was also the goddess of life — and life had to be nurtured.","So, during her stay at the temple, she sometimes allowed herself to think that she was growing closer to War God. That she understood the depths of the boundless love her goddess had for all humans, and especially for War Maidens like her. Eventually, the girls she raised Awakened and left to seek their own devotion. A new generation came to replace them, and she grew to love them as well... but nothing could compare to the bond she felt to her first pupils, and she missed them dearly.","Even if they did not miss her in turn.","The world outside the temple was in turmoil. A new Supreme had recently risen from the clamor of the battlefield and carved out a small empire for himself. His conquest ended swiftly, and he led his warriors home to consolidate and stabilize his Domain.","However, not all of his subjects were satisfied by the promise of peace. Some had greater ambition... some still lusted for blood. His own son slew him and became the new ruler, attaining Supremacy through an act of defiant patricide — and once he began his own conquest, bloodshed never stopped.","His armies spread across the mortal realms like a steel plague, and no one could stop him. One kingdom fell after another, and so did the Supreme rulers of humanity. Eventually, only a few remained, and people began to whisper that the coming of the Second Kingdom was not far away — a kingdom that would unite all humans. A kingdom of blood, a kingdom of murder... a kingdom devoted to nothing but slaying steel.","That was until one of her pupils — her most cherished daughter — led an army of mercenaries to stand in his way.","The news of her death reached the temple long after she perished. The girl had defeated the insurmountable Steel Horde and caused the collapse of the tyrant's Domain. However, in the process, she broke the covenant between her and her goddess... and, as a result, she was cast into the cruelest hell.","On the day the news arrived, the priestesses in the temple were dismayed and angered. Their eyes were full of fury — a War Maiden was meant to die before breaking her oaths, after all. The black sheep of their order had brought them unspeakable shame. However, she felt no fury and no contempt. All she felt was pain and sorrow.","At night, she walked to look at the starlit sky, wondering about the girl she had lost. Had her last moments been painful? Had she suffered? Had she died all alone, surrounded by indifference and scorn?","On that night... she doubted her goddess for the first time.","Soon, she left the temple and returned to the battlefield. The world had descended into chaos after the collapse of the Steel Empire, with countless warlords fighting over its pieces. The Creatures of Corruption raised their monstrous heads and crawled out of the darkness, using the turmoil to reap a rich harvest of human souls.","Rumors were that a new avatar of War God had been born recently somewhere in the mortal realms, and many people believed that an era of bloodshed would begin to welcome the young dragon into the world.","Her life was not much different from how it had been before, when she was younger — and yet, it felt different. Before, she had wandered from one battlefield to another with a sense of purpose. Now, she was simply drifting from one war to another, unbalanced... directionless. Her power was greater than it had ever been, and yet, she felt powerless.","The ancient order of the War Maidens was slowly becoming a vestige of the past, as well. Too many of them had died, and too few were willing to give the oath — the cult of War God was shifting to the worship of a new incarnation of their deity, after all. Those who followed War wanted to submit to the Dragon and serve a living deity, not remake themselves in the image of a distant god.","By then, she had become the greatest warrior of their order, and one with the most prestige as well.","That was when Sun God approached her, beseeching her to become one of Hope's wardens.","“Among the heroes of humanity, I am neither the strongest nor the swiftest. I am not the wisest of us, either. So why me?\"","The avatar of the radiant god remained silent for a long while, then answered in an inscrutable voice.","His answer was simple:","\"Because you never give up.\"","She agreed.","And so, her fate was plucked from the great tapestry and twisted into an endless loop. Taking the remaining War Maidens and those warriors who followed her, she embarked on a journey to the shattered Kingdom of Hope.","She left the world behind.","There, she met the other Chain Lords. The noble Sevirax and his virtuous brother, the enigmatic Saint of Shadows, the aloof oracle who built a temple to the Goddess of the Black Skies in the north, the compassionate and benevolent Aidre... and the eccentric sorcerer, Noctis, as well.","For a while, they performed their duty flawlessly. Outside, the Empire of War expanded through conquest, seamlessly incorporating new lands into its fold. But there was no war in the Kingdom of Hope... there was only time.","Time flowed. People grew old and decrepit, then died. Soon, there was no one left who had known her as she had been before... the priestesses who had raised her were long gone, and her sisters from the temple were gone as well. Even the girls she had nurtured and trained disappeared in the jaws of time, only her memory of them remaining.","She missed them... but she missed the one who had broken the oath the most.","She often went to pray in front of the statue of War God. However, her prayers weren't full of devotion. At times, they were close to sacrilege instead.","\"Why did you abandon her?\"","\"Why was she punished?\"","\"Didn't you love her?\"","\"Didn't your heart bleed while she suffered?\"","“Mine does...\"","She didn't understand why her goddess had been so cruel. She didn't understand how one could love someone, and yet cast their torn and bleeding soul into the depths of hell.","Until, one day, she did.","She understood that gods were different from mortals... and so was their love. So, there was no point in trying to understand it at all.","She laughed bitterly.","She grew despondent.","She allowed herself to question things that she had considered sacred.","During one of the gatherings among the seven immortals, the Beast of Twilight imbibed too much spirit wine, as he always did. The atmosphere was informal, and conversation flowed naturally.","And so, she asked.","“Why do you think the Lord of Light entrusted the keys to Hope's prison to us? Did he want us to protect them? Or did he want us to use them?\"","The eccentric immortal gave her a confused, dazed look.","\"What do you mean, fair maiden? He told us to never let her escape. Surely, that is what he wants.\"","She smiled faintly.","Perhaps she had drunk too much wine, as well.","His answer was reasonable. But was it really so simple?","She shook her head and reached for her cup.","“The gods are not like us. Never trust the gods, Noctis...\"","He didn't seem to hear her, shifting his attention to Lady Aidre of the Heart God's Grove.","The Crimson Beast of Twilight did not pay much attention to their idle chatter, but she couldn't forget.","More time passed, and the world outside fell under the control of the Dragon. And she... she grew tired of her duty. She grew tired of doubt.","She grew tired of her endless life, which was senseless.","She was immortal, after all, so she did not have to struggle to stay alive. There was no war in her life anymore... but there was no peace, either. So, she was neither truly alive nor dead. Everything was meaningless, and she was just stuck in the middle, year after year, burning with a flame that could never go out.","And with each year, that simple question tormented her more and more...","Was their duty to keep Hope imprisoned, or to set her free?","What was Sun God's will, really?","She agonized about it over and over, endlessly. She searched for an answer, but was unable to find it.","Until she realized that the question itself was wrong.","The truth was...","What did she care about Sun God's will? Why was it the will of the gods that mattered?","It didn't.","The only thing that mattered was her will, as well as that of the other Chain Lords. They held the keys to Hope's prison, after all.","So the real question was not what Sun God desired. It was what she desired.","And what she desired... was to free Hope, to give Hope back to the world.","And to herself.","She wanted to be alive again. She wanted to struggle and strive again. She wanted to fight for something that was not meaningless again... to give it her all and walk forward until, one day, she fell short. Until she was defeated and lost her life. She wanted to die.","But fulfilling her desire was not easy.","There were seven Chain Lords, after all, and each of them was both immensely powerful and immortal. She only had one of the seven knives, so she couldn't set Hope free herself — and the others would never agree to betray the order of Sun God.","One day, she was resting in the inner sanctum of the Chalice Temple. In front of her was a stone table, and on its surface stood seven dominoes. She studied them intently, as she did every day for a long, long time.","Finally, she raised a hand and pushed one of the dominoes, watching the rest fall.","A sad smile illuminated her breathtaking, enchantingly radiant face.","The next day, she abandoned her oath and betrayed the War Maidens — she committed a sin that could not be forgiven. Naturally, the other priestesses were not inclined to forgive her. She fought them all — those who were Transcendent or Ascended — killing some and crippling others.","Then, she took her soldiers and left to settle in the west.","Soon after that, she came to push her first domino.","She killed Aidre and burned the sacred grove of Heart God, retrieving the wooden knife that carried her fate.","The other Chain Lords protested, and Noctis came to destroy her.","His wrath shook the heavens, but without the wooden knife, there was little he could do. In the end, seething with hatred, he retreated. The other immortals had no choice but to accept her cruel act, as well. They continued to carry out their duty as Hope's shackles.","But it was already too late.","Because now, there was a crack in the walls of Hope's cage. And through that crack, her influence slowly seeped into the ruins of her once-resplendent kingdom.","Hope slowly drove them all mad.","The noble Sevirax became a horrid, man-devouring monster. His valiant brother became a demented wraith locked inside a molten tomb. The One in the North grew increasingly detached and indifferent, caring not to be alive. The Saint of Shadows stole his fate and killed himself, departing for the Shadow Realm. The Child of the Moon became decadent and unbridled, increasingly manic.","All of them had fallen.","She had fallen, as well.","The descendants of her once-noble warriors degenerated into insane, blood-addled butchers. The pristine Theater of Hope turned into a ghastly sacrificial altar to a misguided facsimile of War. Everything that had been sacred was desecrated, and everything that had been good became foul.","And she... she had gone mad.","At times, she struggled to remember her reasons. Her thoughts twisted, and she became cruel and uncaring. She might have changed her mind a few times...","But it was already too late.","Because once the first domino fell, the rest could not be stopped.","She waited, and waited, and waited...","For someone to win the wooden knife and drive it into her heart.","Countless years passed.","Until, finally, the time arrived for the last domino to topple.","The one who ended it all was Noctis, the Crimson Beast of Twilight. He killed the Sun Prince... he killed the Ivory Lord, Sevirax, as well.","And he defeated her.","Now, finally! Finally! After all these years, after all this torment...","It was her turn to die.","However, fate was not that kind.","And the Beast of Twilight was not that kind, either.","Just when the glorious promise of death was right in front of her, he refused her its embrace.","He chose to sentence her to eternal agony instead.","Trapped in the ruins of a beautiful vessel, her body consumed by a profane vine, she experienced unimaginable pain, indescribable agony. The intolerable bitterness of having no choice but to live, live, live...","Live forever.","Until she outlived everyone... even her beloved goddess. Until she was left utterly, unfathomably alone.","There was only one thing left for her — an eternal, everlasting struggle.","An endless war against the seeds of Corruption that kept blooming in her torn and bleeding soul.","And so, she fought. She endured. She persevered.","Until the entire world was consumed by a hideous tide of nightmares, turning into the cruelest of hells. Until thousands upon thousands of years passed...","Everything was consumed by Corruption. But she wasn't. She alone remained pure.","Because even if there was no hope in the world anymore...","She never gave up."]},{"number":3214,"title":"Chapter 3214 Finest Wine","paragraphs":["Shadow surfaced from the deep pool of memories, feeling a peculiar melancholy. He was not someone to be consumed by emotion, but at the moment, there was a dull ache in his chest. Everything he saw made him feel mournful.","The beauty of the Kingdom of Hope, the majesty of the great theater... and young Noctis.","It was hard to imagine that all these things were fated to become a desolate ruin. The kingdom of Hope would become a shattered land of bloodshed and madness, her pristine white theater would become a ghastly slaughterhouse, and Noctis... Noctis would become one of the chains that bound the Demon of Desire.","Until he was bound and driven mad by eternity, choosing to break her chains. Shadow lowered his gaze.","‘Knowledge... is indeed the heaviest thing in the world.'","A quiet sigh escaped from his lips.","Noctis and Snuggle, meanwhile, were still discussing the play. However, their conversations slowly shifted to the deity who had built it.","\"Do you think we will meet her? The Demon of Desire?\"","Snuggle scoffed.","\"Do you think a goddess is so easy to meet? She is not your grandma, you know! Why would she deign to grace us with her presence?\"","Noctis pointed to Shadow.","\"Isn't he a Supreme Titan? Do you think a goddess wouldn't know that someone like him entered her kingdom, or that his presence was important enough to go take a look?\"","He turned his head.","\"Tell her, Shadow! I bet we will be invited to dine at her palace.\"","Shadow shrugged lightly.","\"Well, I don't know. I doubt it.\"","He lingered for a moment, then added:","\"Also, Hope doesn't have a palace. She has a tower.\"","Noctis grinned.","\"Same thing!\"","The young man seemed excited at the prospect of meeting one of the mythical daemons — despite the fact that people generally feared them, usually far more than the gods. Shadow, however, was not too keen on meeting any deities.","The prospect of meeting Shadow God alone filled him with trepidation.","He wasn't even sure what he was afraid of. Was it being destroyed and sent back into the ocean of endless lives?","Or having his hopes crushed?","He didn't know.","Soon, they returned to the city and found an acceptable inn. The sun was already rolling toward the horizon by then, and night was approaching. Tomorrow, they were going to continue their journey — but tonight, they could simply rest and enjoy each other's company.","The conversation was not flowing, though. Perhaps it was because they knew that there were not a lot of nights like this one left for them, now that they had reached the Kingdom of Hope.","Eventually, Noctis sighed.","“So, what is our plan?\"","Shadow remained silent for a short while.","\"There shouldn't be many problems in a kingdom ruled by a daemon. There will be no Creatures of Corruption to stand in our way, no warring heroes, and no rampaging Spirits to hinder us — no problem that you'll insist that we solve before leaving. So, we can simply head directly north and find a place to cross to the Hollow Mountains.\"","Noctis looked at him with a concerned expression.","He did not have to say anything for Shadow to understand what he felt.","Years ago, Noctis had agreed to be their guide on the way to the Hollow Mountains. He had entertained an ambition to follow them into the Shadow Realm, as well... but, in truth, that was no place for the young Transcendent.","In fact, even the Hollow Mountains themselves were far more than what he could handle. Shadow was not even sure that Snuggle could endure the boundless expanse of nothingness, albeit he was inclined to believe that she could.","Noctis, however... was too young, too untested. As a hero of a divine bloodline, he had achieved Transcendence quite easily — and precisely because he had not struggled enough yet, his claim to existence was tenuous. He didn't even know himself yet, so could he sustain his sense of self in the chilling white mist of the Hollow Mountains?","Unlikely.","That meant that once they reached the Hollow Mountains, they would part ways. Noctis would stay behind, free to live his life as he wanted and continue pursuing excitement and glory. Shadow and Snuggle would continue forward, searching for a way to enter the Underworld.","Needless to say, the young man was disheartened.","Shadow could not say that they had gotten particularly close, but they were not strangers by now, either. As for Noctis and Snuggle — despite their constant bickering, they had long become dear friends. More than that, they were comrades, having fought against countless Creatures of Corruption side by side.","Snuggle sighed.","“Hey, why the long face? It's not like we'll never see each other again.\"","She giggled.","\"After all, Shadow and I are merely going to the Shadow Realm. What's so scary about visiting the Realm of Death? We'll just stay for a bit and come back.\"","Noctis looked at her in dismay.","\"What kind of preposterous...\"","Then, however, he fell silent and stared at her for a few moments.","A faint smile appeared on his face.","\"Then again, knowing you, maybe that is exactly what is going to happen.\"","With a chuckle, Noctis leaned back and studied the strange pair — the man with onyx eyes who wasn't human at all, and a little doll wearing an exquisitely sewn black dress who actually harbored a human soul. He waved to the waiter.","“Good man! More wine. Tonight is a special night, so bring us your best.\"","Noctis sighed.","“Back when I ran away from the temple... I mean, solemnly departed the temple to bring honor to my name... who knew that I would end up this way?\"","He shook his head.","“I went to that mythical realm of yours to slay a powerful Creature of Corruption, but ended up becoming an errand boy for a taciturn Supreme Titan. Strangely enough, though, as an errand boy... I fought and killed more terrifying abominations than any other Transcendent did in these past few years, each of them more terrifying than the previous one. And since the two of you do not like attention, everyone seems to believe that it was the Crimson Beast of Twilight alone who caused all that chaos.\"","Noctis chuckled.","\"Look! It's Noctis, the hero who defeated the Rat. By the gods! It's the Beast of Twilight, who beheaded the Great Demon of the Thousand Steps! Oh my, isn't that Noctis, who obliterated the Devouring Tyrant and its myriad of abominable minions? He's the one who killed the Red Skull Centipede! Who dueled the Transcendent Prince to a stalemate! Who destroyed the Hidden Stronghold and cut down the Bandit King!\"","His expression lacked amusement, but there was a smile on his lips.","Snuggle frowned.","“What are you complaining about? Isn't that what you wanted? To earn a name for yourself and have minstrels sing songs about your astonishing deeds?\"","Noctis hesitated, then shrugged.","\"True, that is what I wanted. I was impatient to prove myself, to let the world know who I am... ah, but somewhere along the way, I seem to have lost that desire.\"","His smile disappeared slowly.","“I am not that same youth anymore, after all. We've been to so many places and seen so many things. The ghastly piles of corpses left in the wake of that Sacred Rat's plague; the gaunt faces of starving children who could not get any food because that damn Great Demon ruined the fields and killed all the merchants. The pitiful ruins of the city devoured by the minions of that Corrupted Tyrant, with no flesh left on the bones of its murdered inhabitants. The monstrous arrogance of Transcendent rulers and those who harbored ambition to rule in their place... and so much more.\"","Noctis looked at Shadow and Snuggle silently for a while, then shook his head.","“Nobody sings about that side of legends. For every name that is known, there is a myriad that disappears forever from the pages of history. So... no, I don't really care about being renowned and famous anymore. I just want to slay Creatures of Corruption and make the lives of all humans a little better. And that is why...\"","He sighed.","“That is why even if you were willing to take me with you on a legendary journey to the Shadow Realm, I would have refused.”","Noctis smiled sadly.","\"There are no humans in the Underworld, after all. There's none in the Shadow Realm, either. So, there is nothing for me to do there. My duty — the duty of an Awakened champion — lies here, in the mortal realms.\"","Finally, the waiter brought the wine to their table. Noctis poured it into three cups and picked up one of them.","\"It just saddens me that we won't be together anymore. Not because I was able to ride on Shadow's shoulders to fame and glory, but because... we are friends.\"","He laughed.","\"You were good friends to me, Snuggle and Shadow. I don't think I'll ever meet friends as good as you. So, thank you.\"","With that, he brought his hands together and gave them a bow. Then, he raised his cup and emptied it in one go.","Shadow hesitated for a moment, then picked up his cup as well.","He smiled faintly.","“There is no need to thank us. Just... make sure that you are a good friend to someone in the future, as well.\"","With that, he drank his wine.","The wine was sweet, and yet it left a bitter aftertaste on his tongue.","Snuggle grasped her cup with both hands and strained a little to raise it a few centimeters above the table.","She remained silent for a moment, her expression solemn.","Then, she glared at Noctis and said with a deep scowl.","“What am I supposed to do with this, you fool? I don't have a mouth! I can't drink wine!\"","Noctis laughed.","Shadow chuckled, as well.","They spent a few more hours chatting and laughing, remembering all the adventures they had experienced during their journey.","That night, when Noctis was already asleep and Snuggle was resting quietly, Shadow sensed something and looked out of the window.","Then, taking a step, he traveled dozens of miles and appeared in front of an old statue depicting the Goddess of War — her primal avatar, who held a spear in one hand and a bleeding human heart in the other.","There was a vague figure standing beneath the statue, wearing a pristine white dress. In the darkness of the night, it was difficult to make out her features... or perhaps her face was simply woven out of night, too sacred and miraculous to be witnessed by mortal eyes.","Shadow hesitated for a moment, then bowed slightly.","“This humble shadow greets Hope, the Demon of Desire... daughter of the Forgotten God.\""]},{"number":3215,"title":"Chapter 3215 Pandora’s Box","paragraphs":["Shadow remained motionless, studying the Demon of Desire with a sense of trepidation.","Most of his senses were useless, as if Hope wasn't there at all. That was because she was suppressing her presence, sparing the world the unfathomable burden of her resplendent divinity — she was known to be a patron of humans, after all. If Hope did not hide her true splendor, merely being near her would have crushed mundane souls. So, Shadow could only see her.","Even then, her figure was nebulous. All he saw was an elegant white dress outlining the shape of a graceful figure, and yet somehow, it felt as if there was nothing beneath the soft fabric at all.","It felt as if the white fabric hid a cosmic infinity, a vast abyss woven out of purest darkness, purest light, and then shaped carelessly to resemble a human.","He shivered, overwhelmed by her breathtaking radiance.","He shuddered, overcome by an alien sense of revulsion.","He felt compelled to fall to his knees in blind worship. He felt his heart drowning in terror, barely suppressing an impulse to flee.","Every emotion, every desire, every passion he had known and tried to forget suddenly ignited with an insurmountable intensity, setting his lightless soul aflame.","Shadow gritted his teeth and suppressed these frenzied flames, pacifying his soul. Just as he did, a voice that sounded like the wind that blew between distant stars and the sound of myriad prayers resounded in the still darkness of the night.","That voice was the most radiant sound he had ever heard, but also the most harrowing.","\"You shouldn't exist.\"","Shadow trembled.","Hope simply shared her thought, but even if she did not put any intent into her words, the world shifted slightly, reshaping itself to fit them. He felt his existence growing a little more vague than it had been before, and had to call upon his Will to solidify it. Only then did Shadow have a chance to consider Hope's words.","‘I.. shouldn't exist?'","It seemed he and the Demon of Desire shared the same thought. Shadow was tired of his endless existence, after all.","Still...","What exactly did she mean by that?","\"Why should I not exist?\"","Hope stood beneath the statue of War God. The statue was illuminated by starlight, while Hope's silhouette was drowning in darkness.","Her nebulous voice resounded again, making the Shadow shiver.","“Because you are not allowed to exist.\"","Taking a step forward, she seemed to study him for a moment.","Then, an ethereal chuckle echoed in the wind.","“And you do not wish to exist, either.\"","Her words sounded certain, but carried a subtle hint of a question.","Shadow frowned, feeling lost. When he sensed the ethereal but irresistible call, he knew that the Demon of Desire had summoned him. But now that he faced her, it was difficult to understand why.","Perhaps it was idle curiosity, no more.","As he considered what to say, Hope turned slightly, looking north.","“The Shadow Realm... that is what you desire?\"","Shadow flinched, feeling like his soul was laid bare in front of her. He hesitated for a moment, then bowed.","“Yes, indeed. That is why I entered your kingdom, my lady. I am merely a traveler passing through.\"","Hope remained motionless, her face still hidden from view. Yet, Shadow felt as if he glimpsed a subtle smile woven out of starlight, glinting in the strange darkness that his sight could not pierce.","“Little shadow, you seem to have forgotten who you are. Do you not wish to remember? If so, I will respect your desire.\"","Suddenly, she was standing just a step away from Shadow, peering into the depths of his being. He felt impossibly small under her gaze... but strangely enough, her attention was not overbearing and crushing. Instead, it was gentle and soothing as a cool spring.","\"But are you sure that you want to face a god? Gods are the reason you are not meant to exist, after all.”","Shadow trembled, but forced himself to remain still. He did not really understand what the Demon of Desire meant... but it seemed that she meant him no harm, at least.","As for her question...","Shadow’s lips slowly twisted into a crooked smile.","“And yet they are the reason I do exist. So, I think gods owe me an explanation.\"","A gust of wind blew across the world, and the tip of War God's spear seemed to glisten in the starlight. Hope's laughter resounded in the darkness, pleasing like the murmur of a clear brook.","\"If so, I will not stop you. Go, little shadow... you have my blessing. May it help your wishes come true.\"","As those words settled in the silence of the night, Shadow felt the world shifting once again, obeying the radiant daemon. Hope's curiosity seemed to be sated. Sparing him one last glance, she turned, as if wanting to leave.","\"Wait!\"","Shadow himself was surprised by his impulsive call. He froze, startled by the sound of his own voice, as well as by the indescribable longing that awoke in his soul when I saw her leave.","Hope did linger for a moment.","He struggled to contain himself for a moment, then asked in a tense, trembling voice:","\"Why... why are you here? Why do you live among humans? Why did you build a kingdom for them, and why do you protect them from the harshness of the world?\"","He did not understand. He could not understand. Even if Shadow was not a god, he had experienced what being worshipped like a god felt like. How deeply it hurt, how inescapable the pain of knowing humans was.","How distasteful human natures were. Whatever he had experienced, Hope would have experienced a thousandfold.","So why would she subject herself to this hideousness, to this torment?","Hope hesitated for a brief moment, then answered in her nebulous, spellbinding voice:","\"Because I am lonely.\"","Turning to Shadow, she laughed quietly.","“All of us are. Isn't that why you are here? Mirage has her illusions; Rime has her flowers. Ariel has his queen, while Nether has his goddess. But I only have humans. I love humans, because they are children of the Flame... and therefore, my children as well.\"","Shadow shook his head in dismay.","Usually, his emotions would not have been so unbridled — but in the presence of Hope, it was impossible to be insincere.","So, he could not stop himself from objecting.","\"But they are so fleeting. As soon as you allow them into your heart, they are gone, leaving you bleeding. How do you save yourself from having to suffer?\"","Hope remained motionless.","Her answer was gentle, as if she was explaining something obvious to a naive child.","\"I simply suffer.\"","She seemed to smile.","“Why would I save myself from sorrow? When I am happy, I savor joy. When I am heartbroken, I savor sorrow. One cannot exist without the other, so only those who know sorrow can experience joy. Little shadow... do you wish to live in a world devoid of happiness?\"","Shadow hesitated, then shook his head slowly.","Hope nodded.","“Then do not save yourself from sorrow.\"","He gritted his teeth, raising his chin in defiance.","“Then what about fury? Human hearts are so hideous, so vile. The crimes they commit are abhorrent; and what is worse, they will commit them in your name. They will desecrate everything that is holy and spoil everything that is pure... there is no end to their ambition, their lust, their greed! When you see all the dirty, dark desires that hide in their hearts, don't you want to erase them from existence and be spared their depravity?\"","The Demon of Desire gazed at him with an emotion that resembled pity.","\"Your two friends, the young wolf pup and the lost soul... are they hideous? Are they vile? Do you feel fury when you are with them, and do you want to erase them from existence?\"","Shadow hesitated, then slowly shook his head.","Hope seemed to smile.","“Humans and gods... all of us are creatures of Desire. Some desires are noble, some are banal, some are twisted and vile. Such is the world. Humans are no different from gods, and gods are no different from humans. If I were to be furious with humans, shouldn't I feel the same fury toward the gods?\"","She shook her head slightly.","“Above all of it, there is choice. Some make the choice to be vile, while some make the choice to be noble. That is what separates us, beings of the Flame — of Desire — from those who have become Corrupted. Because Corruption is the thief of choice.\"","As the stars glistened in the distant sky, Hope shifted, enjoying the warm breeze.","“But not all beings of the Flame are afforded the privilege of making choices, or even knowing that there is a choice. So, all I want to do is help humans learn what they are choosing and help them be in a position to choose. Then, most of them will make the most radiant choices...\"","As the warm breeze reached Shadow, she seemed to smile.","\"...That is my hope.\"","Shadow stared at her, motionless.","Wasn't she saying that she could tolerate the darker side of humanity... for no other reason than that she desired them to choose light?","Because she simply wanted to?","What kind of answer was that?!","Shadow gritted his teeth and then uttered:","“But those humans! Even if gods can endure living in their company, can they endure living alongside gods? Can they survive in the shadow of divinity, doomed to always be lesser, to know that all the things they desire and can never possess belong to someone else?\"","Hope studied him silently for a long while. Eventually, she turned to leave.","\"Then what about us, little shadow? You and I... don't we exist in the shadow of divinity, knowing that all the things we desire belong to someone else?\"","As her nebulous figure disappeared like a fleeting dream, the last echo of her voice caressed his ear like a soothing whisper:","“Don't we daemons live alongside the gods? If we can, why can't humans?\"","A moment later, it was as if she had never been in front of him at all.","Shadow was left alone, standing beneath the statue of War God.","Looking at the bleeding human heart she held in her hand.","He remained silent for a long while, staring at the sharp spear held in the statue's other hand.","Eventually, he asked quietly:","\"Can we?\""]},{"number":3216,"title":"Chapter 3216 Divine Choice","paragraphs":["In the morning, Snuggle and Noctis woke up as if nothing had happened. Listening to their bickering, Shadow did not show that he had conversed with a deity while they slept, either.","He was generally quiet and reserved, so they did not notice his inner turmoil... Noctis did not, at least. Snuggle might have sensed something, but tactfully chose to play along with his silence.","A myriad of thoughts swarmed in Shadow's head.","Had he met a god before?","Across his countless lives, he must have. Yet at the moment, he did not remember — perhaps he had not, after all. The only image in his mind was the harrowing scene of Beast God devouring a Void Creature.","He had been far, far away from that titanic clash, though. Both of those beings were simply so colossal that they could be seen from a vast distance. If Shadow had been any closer, he would have been obliterated by the violent horror of the divine confrontation.","The daemons were not equal to the great gods, but by now, they were Divine. So, for Shadow, meeting Hope was no different from facing true divinity for the first time. Needless to say, she had not disappointed his expectations.","Even if Hope had been suppressing her deific presence to the point that it was all but impossible to sense her existence, her visage had still left a profound impression on Shadow. He could not even describe the feeling she had invoked in him... it was simply too compelling, too poignant. Unknowable.","And he was a vast being on the precipice of becoming a deity himself, at that. Shadow could not even imagine the awe those lesser than him would feel in her presence. Perhaps that was why she concealed it and obscured her visage — because she wanted those whom she met to feel emotions other than awe. To look past her divinity and see her instead.","Unlike Shadow, who hid because he didn't want to be seen.","Beyond the shock of witnessing the Demon of Desire, though, were the words that she had spoken.","Shadow was surprised to learn that Hope was such an... optimist.","Perhaps there was a seed of profound wisdom in what she had told him, but he felt reluctant to accept it. That was because Hope did not know the future — but he did. She had told him that if daemons could live alongside the gods, then humans could too. And yet, all of existence was doomed to be destroyed in a war between the gods and the daemons.","Didn't that make Hope's conviction misguided and naive?","As Shadow and his companions departed from the inn and left the city, Shadow contemplated deeply.","‘No... perhaps not.'","Hope did not strike Shadow as someone who could be naive, let alone misguided. So perhaps what she meant was not that the daemons and the gods were coexisting splendidly, so humans could too. Because they were all the same. Because they were all children of the Flame.","Perhaps what she truly meant had to do with everything she had said before.","Perhaps it was that daemons had a choice, just like humans... just like the gods.","And that she hoped they would choose wisely.","...However, in the end, her hope was destined to be crushed.","It was destined to be crushed by Nether, the Demon of Choice.","Who chose war.","As Shadow was jostled lightly on the coachman's bench, he sighed.","‘Well. It's not like that has anything to do with me.'","Shadow seemed like a vast and unfathomable being to someone like Noctis or Snuggle. But to beings like Hope or the great gods, he was no more than a little, transient shadow.","Gods were great, but Shadow was small. He had no business concerning himself with the fate of the gods and the choices of daemons. All he wanted to do was keep a promise he should have given a dear friend, but never had — and then, perhaps, find a way to end his tedious existence.","‘It is quite ironic, isn't it?'","The Demon of Desire, who called herself Hope, was destined to have her hopes crushed.","And Shadow, a creature of death, wanted to die but did not know how.","‘We really are quite a pair.'","Perhaps that was why he had sensed a hint of affection in the way Hope spoke to him.","“What are you thinking about, Shadow?\"","Snuggle's squeaky voice pulled him out of his contemplation.","Pulling slightly on the reins of their horse, Shadow smiled faintly and shook his head.","\"I was wondering if the Demon of Desire likes me.\"","Both Noctis and Snuggle stared at him, their mouths agape — one of their mouths, at least.","In the end, Noctis exhaled slowly and gave him a thumbs up.","His hand seemed to be trembling.","\"Please forgive me, Brother Shadow. I did not know that you are a man of great ambition. This junior still has a lot to learn... I've never even dared to think about aiming that high...\"","Snuggle seemed to have regained her composure, as well. She looked at him tearfully.","“Our Shadow is all grown up! He likes girls now... well, primordial deities, at least...\"","Shadow sighed.","“You two are fools.\"","Snuggle giggled, while Noctis exploded with laughter.","\"That we are, that we are...\"","***","Their journey north was uneventful.","There were no powerful Creatures of Corruption in the Kingdom of Hope. There were no Transcendent warriors searching for trouble or rampaging Spirits, either. The roads were well-maintained, and the weather was gentle. Their carriage rolled forward at a steady pace, devouring mile after mile.","Without having to hurry, they reached the northernmost edges of the Kingdom of Hope in a few weeks. Those weeks were blissful and carefree, full of nothing but leisure — none of them spoke about the inevitable parting, which was drawing near. In the end, however, that day still arrived. The carriage stopped near a vast meadow, a modest mountain chain looming far in the distance. A warm breeze blew across the meadow, making the grass ripple like the waves of an emerald sea. The sun was shining high in the sky, and there was no cloud in sight to obscure it.","It was only when they alighted from the carriage and gazed at the horizon that Noctis finally lost his smile, looking ahead with a dejected expression.","Snuggle remained silent for a while, then tentatively pulled on the hem of his colorful robe.","“I meant it. There is no need to feel sad. We will definitely meet again, someday.\"","Noctis stared into the distance, his face solemn.","Eventually, he shook his head.","“No, it's not that. I just... realized something only now. When it's already too late.\"","Shadow and Snuggle looked at him quietly, giving the young man time to speak.","After a while, Noctis let out a long sigh.","“I realized that once Shadow leaves...\"","His face hardened.","\"This damn horse will disappear. So I'll have to either abandon this wonderful carriage or pull it myself. By the Moon! What a travesty!\"","As he looked at the luxurious carriage, his expression turned mournful.","His lips even quivered a little.","Shadow stared at him for a bit, then patted him on the shoulder.","\"Stay strong.”","Snuggle nodded seriously.","“Our thoughts will be with you. You can endure!\"","Noctis looked down, hiding a smile.","When he looked up, however, there were traces of genuine sadness in his eyes.","“What are you doing? Go. We have already said everything that needed to be said... trying to pull off an emotional farewell will only be awkward. It's been a pleasure traveling with you, friends. But there are countless other pleasures to be enjoyed in the world, and I am off to enjoy them all by myself. If anything, you are the one who should wallow in sadness and envy.\"","Shadow smiled faintly.","\"Perhaps we will.\"","Then, he looked back at the radiant vista of the Kingdom of Hope.","\"So, what are your plans? Are you going to stay here for a while and explore Hope's domain?\"","Noctis shook his head slowly.","\"No. You saw it yourself — there are no dreadful abominations or bloodthirsty villains in the Kingdom of Hope. I am not needed here. So, I'll go someplace where a fool like me can be of use.\"","He sighed, then beamed them a smile.","\"I'll go be a hero... no different from all the other Transcendent heroes, but far more handsome and with better style. Be prepared! You may hear about my incredible deeds and astonishing looks even in the Shadow Realm.\"","He hesitated for a moment.","“But what about you? Are you sure that you want to continue forward? The Hollow Mountains, the Underworld, and the Realm of Death itself... as far as itineraries go, that one sounds like a real drag. You might want to consider a better pastime.\"","Shadow chuckled.","“We'll be fine. I've been to all those places before, I think... a long time ago. We'll manage.\"","Noctis studied him for a long while, then nodded.","\"In that case, go. I wish you luck on your journey. And now that I think about it...\"","He fell silent for a brief moment, then nodded decisively.","\"I think I'll drag that carriage to the nearest settlement, after all. Surely, I'll be able to buy a horse there! Luxurious coaches like this one don't just grow on trees, you know.\"","Shadow smiled.","“It depends on the tree, I guess.\"","As he turned to face the distant mountains, Snuggle climbed to Noctis's shoulder and hugged him tightly. She whispered something into his ear, causing him to laugh, then jumped down and scampered over to Shadow.","Picking her up, he prepared to cross the realm boundary and enter the Hollow Mountains.","The last leg of their journey awaited ahead. Just before the pull of a different realm grasped him, Shadow turned his head and looked at the young man who stood behind them.","\"Noctis...\"","Shadow lingered for a moment, struggling with something, and then finally said:","\"Do not let yourself be bound, Noctis. Wolves... are meant to be free.\"","In the next moment, the warmth of the Kingdom of Hope disappeared, replaced by a chilling cold.","The radiant vista of the emerald meadow was gone, as well.","Instead, Shadow and Snuggle were surrounded by swirling white fog, unable to see anything.","As if nothing existed in the world anymore, except for the two of them — and the endless expanse of swirling mist."]}]);
